hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Bishr ibn Ubayd al-Darisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Ataki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlook the sin of the generous, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic takes his hand at his stumble. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Muhammad ibn Humayd; Bishr alone narrated it from him."
"1202","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: A woman came to me and I brought her food, and she said: I am fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it makeup for Ramadan? She said: No. He said: Then break your fast and make up in its place. No one narrated this hadith from Amrah except Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, nor from Abdullah except Abu Ubaydah; Yaqub alone narrated it from him."
"1203","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Yahya ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Dakhil ibn Isa ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Shayban narrated to me, from Ali ibn Yazid, from his father Yazid ibn Ali, from his father Ali ibn Shayban that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him and said: O Allah, bless Ali ibn Shayban, and bless upon Ali. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Miskin alone narrated it."
"1204","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Zayd al-Harawi Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Zayd; Ubaydullah alone narrated it from him."
"1205","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Samman Ashath ibn Said narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will increase, and my Companions will decrease, so do not revile them; whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Abu al-Rabi and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah; Abdullah ibn Muawiyah alone narrated it from Abu al-Rabi."
"1206","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Thabit, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the image-makers on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you created. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Thabit al-Ansari except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal alone narrated it from him."
"1207","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Hani ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Hani; Ubaydullah ibn Jarir alone narrated it from him."
"1208","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Concerning buried treasure, the fifth."
"1209","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his mother and from his sister, from Aishah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to walk to the House. He said: Order your sister to ride, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic is free from your sister torturing herself. The man said: My mother owes Hajj, shall I perform Hajj for her? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"1210","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was occupied with some matter of the polytheists, so he did not pray Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha; when he finished he prayed them afterwards, the first first, and that was before the fear prayer was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman except Layth; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone narrated it from him."
"1211","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Nuaym al-Sawwaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zibyan, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan ibn Thabit: Lampoon the polytheists, and Jibril is with you. No one narrated it from Sufyan except Abdullah ibn Jafar."
"1212","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simmari narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Awf ibn Muhammad Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar who said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulate after the dawn prayer, then pray two rakahs, then say: Prayer is disliked only at sunrise, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Muhammad; Awf alone narrated it from him."
"1213","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Adam ibn Ali that he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fruit is not to be sold until it ripens. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Dawud; Abu al-Jawza alone narrated it from him."
"1214","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawza narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqyah, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurrah except Abu Ali al-Hanafi Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid; Abu al-Jawza alone narrated it from him."
"1215","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Ata, from Aishah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing and sitting, praying wearing sandals and barefoot, and turning from prayer to his right and to his left."
"1216","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his wives a choice, and it was not a divorce. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Khalid; Muhammad alone narrated it from him."
"1217","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the mujahid in the path of Allah, or like the one who stands at night and fasts by day; and the guardian of the orphan - his own or another's - when he fears Allah the Mighty and Majestic, I and he will be in Paradise like these two, meaning his index and middle fingers. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except al-Fadl."
"1218","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar concerning this verse: Take pardoning, he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic commanded His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to take pardoning from the conduct of people. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from Ibn Umar except al-Tufawi."
"1219","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except al-Arzami, nor from al-Arzami except Abu Bakr; Azhar alone narrated it from him."
"1220","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah who said: I wrote to Ibrahim al-Nakhai asking him about suckling, and in his letter was that Abu al-Shatha al-Muharibi narrated to him that Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One sucking nor two suckings make unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said."
"1221","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and from Muslim, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah except Ziyad."
"1222","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Humayd, from Ata, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loses his sight in this world, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will make for him a light on the Day of Resurrection if he was righteous. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Bishr ibn Ibrahim al-Ansari."
"1223","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Salim al-Aftas, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The muezzin who seeks reward is like the martyr wallowing in his blood, wishing from Allah whatever he desires between the adhan and the iqamah. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Qays; Ibrahim alone narrated it from him."
"1224","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it, and if the month is obscured for you, complete the number as thirty. No one narrated this hadith from Hajjaj except Yahya."
"1225","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Abdullah al-Absi al-Kufi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's spending upon his dependents is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Mumin except Muhammad."
"1226","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi al-Hawajib al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: I was holding the hand of al-Amash and he said: I recited the Quran to Yahya ibn Waththab thirty times, each time reciting: And al-Rujz, and likewise Yahya recited to Alqamah, and Alqamah to Ibn Masud, and Ibn Masud to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ibn Abi al-Hawajib."
"1227","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best jihad is one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Abu Bahr."
"1228","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Mutamir."
"1229","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Yazid Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The expiation of a gathering is that the servant says after standing: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ubayd and al-Nadr ibn Kathir."
"1230","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from his father that a man came to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him about something, so Zayd said to him: Go to Abu Hurayrah, for while I and Abu Hurayrah and so-and-so were one day in the mosque, supplicating and remembering our Lord the Mighty and Majestic, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us until he sat with us, and we fell silent, so he said: Return to what you were engaged in. Zayd said: So I and my companion supplicated before Abu Hurayrah, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying amen to our supplication; then Abu Hurayrah supplicated and said: O Allah, I ask You for what my two companions asked You, and I ask You for knowledge that is not forgotten. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Amen. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we ask Allah for knowledge that is not forgotten. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dawsi boy has preceded you with it. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except al-Fadl, and it is not narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit except with this chain."
"1231","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Marwan Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a camel on the day of the conquest, with him a hooked staff with which he would touch the Corner, out of dislike that people be struck away from him. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Yahya and Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi."
"1232","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change gray hair and do not resemble the Jews and the Christians. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Muhammad."
"1233","With the same chain, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer at the time he commits it, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer at the time he steals, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer at the time he drinks it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Muhammad."
"1234","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Umar ibn Salit narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Abu Wail, from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of merchants, idle talk and oaths attend your sales, so mix them with something of charity. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah al-Awar Maymun except Hammad; Ishaq alone narrated it from him."
"1235","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there did not remain of this world except one day, Allah would lengthen that day until He sends a man from my household, his name corresponding to my name and his father's name to my father's name; he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with wrong and injustice. No one narrated this hadith from Zaidah except Ubaydullah."
"1236","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Mutamir."
"1237","Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, sincerely, will enter Paradise. It was said: And what is its sincerity? He said: That it restrains him from the prohibitions of Allah the Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Sharik; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it from him."
"1238","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Raddad Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, he said: Abu Zarah Wahbullah ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man says to a man: O disbeliever, disbelief has become binding upon one of them. No one narrated this hadith from Haywah except Wahbullah."
"1239","With the same chain: Haywah narrated to us, from Khayr ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the cat. No one narrated this hadith from Haywah except Wahbullah."
"1240","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bakr al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: My uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would command them to use the siwak with every ablution. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1241","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Maghrib with: Those who disbelieve and bar from the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Abu Muawiyah; al-Husayn alone narrated it from him."
"1242","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Ajlan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makhzumi, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The servant seeks the pleasure of Allah the Mighty and Majestic and continues thus, so Allah says: O Jibril, My servant so-and-so seeks to please Me, so My pleasure is upon him. He said: So Jibril (peace be upon him) says: The mercy of Allah upon so-and-so, and the bearers of the Throne say it, and those next to them say it, until the inhabitants of the seven heavens say it, then it descends to the earth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And it is the verse Allah revealed to you in His Book: Indeed those who believe and do righteous deeds, the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection; and the servant seeks the wrath of Allah, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: O Jibril, so-and-so angers Me, indeed My anger is upon him; so Jibril says: Allah is angry with so-and-so, and the bearers of the Throne say it, and those below them say it, until the inhabitants of the seven heavens say it, then it descends to the earth. This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; Maymun alone narrated it."
"1243","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with three, reciting in the first: Rivalry in increase diverted you, and: Indeed We sent it down, and: When shaken; and reciting in the second al-Asr, and: Indeed We gave you al-Kawthar, and: When the help of Allah comes; and in the third: Say, O disbelievers, and: Perish, and: Say, He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yazid and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq; Yaqub alone narrated it from Yazid, and Yunus ibn Bukayr from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq."
"1244","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muammil ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab concerning His saying the Mighty and Majestic: And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment before the greater punishment, he said: Calamities of this world, he said: And the Smoke has passed. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Badal."
"1245","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Salman al-Farisi who said: I brought zakat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times. And he said: Whom do you count as martyrs among you? They said: The one killed in the path of Allah. He said: The martyrs of my ummah would then be few: being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the plague is martyrdom, the woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, consumption is martyrdom, and abdominal illness is martyrdom. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Mindal; Bakr alone narrated it from him."
"1246","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from a man of the people of Sham, meaning al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, from Abu Dharr al-Ghifari who said: I was indeed present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a circle, and in his hand were pebbles, and they glorified Allah in his hand, and among us were Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali, and those in the circle heard their glorification; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed them to Abu Bakr, and they glorified with Abu Bakr, and those in the circle heard their glorification; then they were handed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they glorified in his hand; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed them to Umar, and they glorified in his hand, and those in the circle heard their glorification; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed them to Uthman ibn Affan, and they glorified in his hand; then he handed them to us, and they did not glorify with any of us. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Humayd; al-Jarudi alone narrated it from his father."
"1247","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah who said: Among what Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: Allah indeed tests the servant while He loves him, to hear his humble supplication."
"1248","With the same chain: Shubah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, the like of it. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Jabir; Abu Hatim alone narrated it from him."
"1249","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Abbas who said: Nabidh would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the evening, and he would drink it that night and day, and night and day, and night and day; then when evening came he would give it to the servants or pour it out. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya except Yazid; Yaqub alone narrated it from him, while Sufyan al-Thawri and Sharik narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas."
"1250","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he would say: To You I submit myself, and to You I entrust my affair, and to You I lay my back, hoping and fearing You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in the Book You sent down, and in the Messenger You sent. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Thabit, nor from Thabit except Hammad; Muammil alone narrated it from him."
"1251","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zakariyya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together in eating, except that one of you seeks permission from his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Said."
"1252","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from his father, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Jafar ibn Abi Talib to Abyssinia, he accompanied him and provided him with these words: O Allah, be gentle to me in easing every difficulty, for easing every difficulty is easy for You, and I ask You for ease and well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"1253","With the same chain: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Allah the Mighty and Majestic boasted to His angels about His servants on the evening of Arafah in general, and boasted about Umar ibn al-Khattab in particular. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Ala except Abd al-Rahman; his son alone narrated them from him."
"1254","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Ubaydah al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: My father said: O Prophet of Allah, I perform ablution and touch my private part? He said: It is part of you."
"1255","With the same chain: from Asad who said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man eat with his left hand and drink with his left hand."
"1256","With the same chain: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"1257","With the same chain: from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"1258","With the same chain: from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah who said: We were forbidden from following funerals, but it was not made binding upon us."
"1259","With the same chain: from Asad, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman in a litter, with her a son of hers; she raised her head and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and for you a reward. No one narrated these hadiths from Asad except Khalaf; Ali alone narrated them from him."
"1260","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I heard Harun ibn Ishaq saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad saying: Sufyan al-Thawri passed by Asad ibn Ubaydah and greeted him, and it was as if Asad did not return the greeting, so Sufyan returned to him and said: O Asad, I pass by you and greet you, yet you do not return; so he apologized to him that he was occupied, and it was as if Sufyan was not satisfied with that from him. So Asad said to him: O Sufyan, how has your rank reached that I should know of Allah other than what you know. Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah said: Khalaf ibn Tamim, Zafir ibn Sulayman, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated from Asad ibn Ubaydah."
"1261","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father, from al-Hakam, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mutim, from al-Bara ibn Azib and Zayd ibn Arqam who both said: The Messenger of Allah forbade that silver be sold for gold on credit. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Sulayman."
"1262","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kab al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Shuqran narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before him, and trembling seized him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Calm yourself, for I am not a king; I am only the son of a woman of Quraysh who used to eat dried meat. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail, from Qays, from Jarir except Isa; Shuqran alone narrated it from him."
"1263","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qarni narrated to us, he said: Bishr al-Ummi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from al-Walid ibn Bukayr, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Adawi, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has made Friday obligatory upon you, from this day of mine, in this year of mine, in this month of mine, an enjoined obligation; whoever abandons it out of aversion to it, while having a just or unjust imam, then may Allah not gather his affair, nor bless him in his matter; indeed he has no prayer, indeed he has no zakat, indeed he has no fasting, indeed he has no Hajj; indeed no woman shall lead a man, nor shall a Bedouin lead an emigrant, nor shall a wicked man lead a righteous one, except a ruler whose sword and whip are feared. No one narrated this hadith from Bishr al-Ummi except Khalid ibn Yazid; Ibrahim ibn Rashid alone narrated it from him; and no supported hadith of Bishr al-Ummi is remembered other than this, and he was among the righteous servants of Allah."
"1264","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Qurashi saying: I said to Maruf al-Karkhi: O Abu Mahfuz, have I seen in this land a person who has approached the rank of the Abdal? He fell silent, then said: O Allah, except that one called Bishr al-Ummi. Muhammad ibn Mansur said: I heard Khalaf ibn Tamim saying: Bishr al-Ummi said: Brothers upon generosity are more beloved to us than brothers upon ease."
"1265","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhayyah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Ashari said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will come upon people a cleaving trial that leaves the wise bewildered; the sleeping one in it is better than the sitting, the sitting in it is better than the standing, the standing in it is better than the walking, and the walking in it is better than the hastening. So cut your bowstrings and break swords with stones. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Abu al-Muhayyah; Abu Hammam alone narrated it from him."
"1266","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two should go out to relieve themselves, sitting conversing, uncovering their private parts, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic is angry at that. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah except Ubayd, while Sufyan al-Thawri and others narrated it from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Iyad ibn Hilal, from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"1267","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd narrated to me, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Maruf ibn Bashir narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade soaking in gourds, hantam, naqir, and varnished vessels. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Ubayd."
"1268","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ata, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever comes to Friday, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Hassan alone narrated it from him."
"1269","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab Jafar ibn al-Harith al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman the freedman of the family of Talhah, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Hassan alone narrated it from him."
"1270","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim al-Adawi al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Bakr al-Mawsili narrated to me, he said: Zakariyya ibn Isa al-Shabi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Nafi informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give the charity of fitr as a sa of dates or a sa of barley."
"1271","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Nafi informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Hafsah the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the caller called for the dawn prayer would pray two light rakahs."
"1272","With the same chain: Nafi informed me that a man of the Ansar informed him that Kab ibn Ujrah suffered harm in his head and shaved, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to offer a sacrificial cow as hadi."
"1273","With the same chain: from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another valley, and nothing fills his mouth except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"1274","With the same chain, he said: Ibn Shihab said: And Said ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; whoever says: There is no god but Allah, has protected from me his wealth and self except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah the Mighty and Majestic; and Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed in His Book, mentioning that a people were arrogant, saying: Indeed they, when it was said to them: There is no god but Allah, would be arrogant; and Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: When those who disbelieved put in their hearts the zeal, the zeal of ignorance, Allah sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger and upon the believers, and imposed upon them the word of righteousness, and they were more deserving of it and worthy of it, and it is: There is no god but Allah."
"1275","With the same chain, he said: Ibn Shihab said: And Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I would love to fight in the path of Allah, then be killed, then be brought to life, then be killed, then be brought to life."
"1276","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting, so a man of the Muslims said: But you fast continuously. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And which of you is like me? I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink; when they refused to stop continuous fasting, he fasted continuously with them a day, then a day, then they saw the crescent, so he said: If it had been delayed, I would have added for you, as one disciplining them when they refused to stop. No one narrated these hadiths from Zakariyya except Umar; Abu al-Qasim al-Adawi alone narrated them from him."
"1277","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Husayn al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: Qatadah ibn al-Fadl ibn Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Sharawi, from Ata, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Give glad tidings to those who walk to mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Aishah except al-Hasan; Qatadah alone narrated it from him."
"1278","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Khalid ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ubaydullah ibn al-Rabi, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying Duha six rakahs, and I have not abandoned them since. Al-Hasan said: And I have not abandoned them since."
"1279","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Preemption is for the partner and the neighbor until they leave it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Ibn Dhi Himayah."
"1280","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind that al-Hasan would narrate that Qays ibn Ubad and Ibn al-Kawwa were with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and they were wounded on the day of Siffin, so he said: For what do we kill ourselves? Come with us to this man to ask him: Was this upon the covenant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or an opinion he held? He said: So we went until we came to him, and said: Wounds reach us as you see, and we remind you by Allah and Islam: Is this something the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon you, or an opinion you held? He said: What do you want with this? They said: We remind you by Allah and Islam, twice or thrice. He said: Rather an opinion I held, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me nothing concerning it; but Uthman was killed, and the people pledged allegiance, and I saw that I was most deserving of it. They said to him: For what do we shed our lifeblood upon the opinions of men? So they sat in their houses. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Abd al-Aziz; al-Walid alone narrated it from him."
"1281","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ziyad al-Naji narrated to us, he said: I was with Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas - and with him a man - when he was brought a small son of his brother Jafar, and he seated him in his lap, stroking his head thus from front to back, turning his hair; the boy became annoyed, so the man with him said to him: May Allah set right the amir, the boy is annoyed. He said: Be silent; Abu Ayyub narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdullah ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the boy is an orphan, wipe his head thus toward the front, and when he has a father, wipe his head thus toward the back from the front. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sulayman except Salih; Muhammad ibn Sudran alone narrated it from him."
"1282","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sadl in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Amir except Said; Abu Bahr alone narrated it from him."
"1283","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muammil ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: I gave a she-camel in the path of Allah, then wanted to buy from its offspring, or he said: from its progeny, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Leave it until it comes on the Day of Resurrection, it and its offspring together, in your scale. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Muammil."
"1284","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Wasil the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man of Quraysh approached; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought him near and honored him; when he stood, he said: O Buraydah, do you know this one? I said: Yes, this is the most middle of Quraysh in lineage and the most of them in wealth, thrice; then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I informed you of my knowledge of him, and you know best. He said: This is among those for whom Allah will establish no weight on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Hisham; Awn alone narrated it from him."
"1285","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas concerning the saying of Allah: He knows the treachery of the eyes: When you look at it, do you intend treachery or not? And what breasts conceal: When you are able over it, will you fornicate with it or not? Shall I not inform you of what follows it: And Allah judges with truth: Able to reward good with good and evil with evil; indeed Allah is the Hearing, the Seeing. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"1286","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Manjufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhazzam Yazid ibn Sufyan al-Tamimi narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the seventeenth, or nineteenth, or twenty-first, or twenty-third, or twenty-fifth, or twenty-seventh, or twenty-ninth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Muhazzam except Sulaym."
"1287","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Muammil ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was occupied on the day of the Trench from the Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha prayers, so he commanded Bilal, who called the adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Dhuhr; then he commanded him, so he called adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Asr; then he commanded him, so he called adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Maghrib; then he commanded him, so he called adhan and iqamah, and he prayed Isha; then he said: There is no people upon the face of the earth remembering Allah at this hour besides you. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Muammil."
"1288","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawaa narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Salamah, from Aban ibn al-Qasim, from al-Harith al-Awar who said: I entered upon Ali after Isha, and he said: What brings you at this hour? I said: I love you. He said: By Allah, do you love me? I said: Yes, by Allah I love you. He said: Shall I not teach you a supplication the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me? I said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, open the hearing of my heart to Your remembrance, and grant me obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger, and action by Your Book. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Sawaa alone narrated it from him."
"1289","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: I indeed saw myself before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the bed, at the place of a funeral, while he prayed; I disliked standing fully facing him, so I would slip away from beside the legs of the bed. And I indeed saw myself with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, with upon me and upon him one garment. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except al-Fadl."
"1290","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Said ibn Muslim, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank while standing. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Isa, nor from Isa except Hashim and Muammil ibn al-Fadl."
"1291","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muhammad, when you see people fighting over this world, strike your sword upon the greatest rock in al-Harrah until it breaks, then sit in your house until an erring hand or a decreed death comes to you. So I did what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Maslamah alone narrated it from him."
"1292","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: By Allah, I am no more entitled to this wealth than any of you, but according to our stations in the Book of Allah and the distribution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no Muslim except he has a known share in this wealth, given to him or withheld, except an owned slave. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Maslamah alone narrated it from him."
"1293","Abu Bakr Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muslim al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the expedition of Tabuk on Thursday, and he loved to go out on Thursday. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj, from Mamar except Hajjaj."
"1294","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Ubaydullah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Hajjaj."
"1295","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: al-Asmai narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave a gathering I sat in during disbelief except I proclaim Islam in it; so he came to the mosque, in which were groups of Quraysh sitting in circles, and began proclaiming Islam and testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The polytheists rose, beating him and being beaten by him; when they outnumbered him, a man rescued him. I said to Umar: Who is the man who rescued you from the polytheists? He said: That is al-As ibn Wail al-Sahmi. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except al-Asmai; Abu Hatim alone narrated it from him."
"1296","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mahfuz ibn Bahr al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hand me the khumrah. I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except al-Walid."
"1297","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Shabi, from al-Bara ibn Azib that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of sacrifice without adhan or iqamah, then addressed the men, then stood toward the women, addressed them and urged them to charity, until much goods gathered with Bilal. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Ubaydah; Abdullah ibn Umar alone narrated it from him."
"1298","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muslim al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ghaylan ibn Jami narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi who said: Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai narrated to me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Jam, with people around him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the mountain of Tayy, and I have wearied myself and my mount; by Allah, I left no rope except I stood upon it. Is there Hajj for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever attains with us the dawn prayer at Jam, having already poured forth from Arafat before that by night or day, has completed his rites and his Hajj is complete. No one narrated this hadith from Ghaylan except Yala, nor from Yala except his son; Ali alone narrated it from him."
"1299","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas - I think he raised it - who said: None of you should say: I am sarurah. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan as raised except Muawiyah."
"1300","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Khubayq al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Ali al-Muqri narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat who said: I said to al-Amash: They object to our reading of two letters: Ma antum bi musrikhiyya and another letter. He said: Inform them that I recited to al-Amash, and that al-Amash recited to Yahya ibn Waththab, and that Yahya recited it to Alqamah, and that Alqamah recited to Abdullah, and that Abdullah recited to the Messenger of Allah; so whoever has such a chain like this upon him... they come."
"1301","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hudayr, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from al-Mughirah who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and I saw him relieve himself, then return and perform ablution, wiping over his khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad except Abdullah ibn Hudayr."
"1302","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Zaidah Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from Abu Burdah that Abu Musa entered upon al-Hasan ibn Ali visiting him, and Ali said to him: Have you come to us visiting, O Abu Musa, or visiting my brother's son? He said: No, rather I came visiting. Ali said: I indeed heard him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits, it envelops him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hayyan except al-Muharibi; Abu Zaidah alone narrated it from him."
"1303","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Baalbakki narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, my ummah among them eighty rows, and the rest of the nations forty rows. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah except Zuhayr; Suwayd alone narrated it from him."
"1304","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the muezzin established prayer while he was eating, would not stand until he finished his food."
"1305","With the same chain, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make Madinah beloved to us as our love for Makkah or more intense; O Allah, bless for us our sa and our mudd, and transfer its fever to al-Juhfah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sufyan except Muawiyah."
"1306","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Sabbah, the freedman of al-Husayn, narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Sufyan and Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for perhaps one it is conveyed to retains more than the hearer. No one narrated this hadith from Huraym and Ja'far except Ishaq."
"1307","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Isl ibn Sufyan, from al-Salil, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Never does the star rise in the morning while a people suffer a blight except it is lifted from them. No one among those who narrated this hadith from Isl ibn Sufyan and from Ata entered al-Salil except Wuhayb, nor from Wuhayb except Harami; al-Jarrah is alone in it."
"1308","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In every prayer there is recitation: the Opening of the Book and what is easy, and whoever does not recite, it is deficient. No one narrated this hadith from Said with this wording except Said; Ibn Abi Safwan is alone in it."
"1309","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Abd Allah."
"1310","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Salamah al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Matar al-Warraq and Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Amir al-Ahwal, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his Companions while they were disputing about the Decree, each citing a verse against the other, so it was as if pomegranate seeds had burst upon his face, and he said: Is this what you were commanded, to strike parts of the Book of Allah against one another? Look to what you were commanded and follow it, and what you were forbidden, avoid it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammad; Jafar ibn Salamah is alone in it."
"1311","Abu Bakr Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn al-Fadl, the brother of Arim, narrated to us, he said: Arim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you lives will soon see Isa son of Maryam as a just leading imam; the jizyah will be abolished, the cross broken, the pig killed, and war will lay down its burdens. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Hammad; Bistam is alone in it."
"1312","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Nasai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, that Abu Musa al-Ashari lost consciousness, and the daughter of Abu Dumah, his wife, wept over him, then he recovered and said: I disavow whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disavowed: whoever shaves, or wails loudly, or tears garments. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abd al-Samad."
"1313","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic, nor more effective, than: Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak; if you can, do not abandon it, then do so."
"1314","And with the same chain: Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sad, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you hear of plague in a land, do not enter it, and if it occurs while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abd al-Hamid except Umayr."
"1315","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ask for leadership, for if you ask for it and are given it, you will be left to yourself, and if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it; and if you swear an oath and see something else better than it, do what is better and expiate your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Abu Bahr."
"1316","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Umarah al-Miwali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat twice in one day. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah except Muslim."
"1317","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli, from Jafar al-Ahmar, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge and accepted deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Jafar, nor from Jafar except Ishaq; Husayn ibn Ali is alone in it, from his father."
"1318","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi say: al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us, and he was not untruthful, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed with them and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, they did not raise their heads from bowing to stand until they saw him prostrate. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from al-Hakam, except Muhammad ibn Ararah; Muhammad ibn al-Layth is alone in it."
"1319","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None loves the Ansar except a believer, and none hates them except a hypocrite. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, except Muhammad ibn Ararah; Muhammad ibn al-Layth is alone in it, and the well-known version is from Shubah from Adi ibn Thabit."
"1320","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Taifi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage is a bond of lineage; it is neither sold nor granted."
"1321","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling clientage and granting it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ismail except Yahya."
"1322","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Hashim al-Bazzaz narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Burd, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will ward off His punishment from him, and whoever guards his tongue, Allah will conceal his faults. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Khalid, nor from Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Hilal is alone in it."
"1323","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it while relieving himself, a good deed is recorded for him and a bad deed erased from him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Husayn, nor from Husayn except Ibrahim, nor from Ibrahim except al-Qasim; Ahmad ibn Harb is alone in it."
"1324","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Misar, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, performed ablution, then prayed eight rakahs, then prayed witr with three, then lay down. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Waki; al-Husayn is alone in it."
"1325","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Is jihad incumbent upon women? He said: Their jihad is the Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ibn Fudayl; Ali is alone in it."
"1326","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Rafiqi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi and Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: I heard al-Rabi ibn Sabrah narrating, from his father, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, people said: Enjoy mutah. So I and a cousin of mine went out, he had a cloak and I had a cloak. We proposed to a woman in Makkah; his cloak was better than mine, while I was more handsome and younger. She said: A cloak for a cloak, but one man handsomer than the other. So I married her and consummated with her, then I returned to find the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing, saying: I had permitted mutah for you, but Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and informed me it is forbidden until the Day of Resurrection; whoever among you has entered upon a woman, let him not return to her, and do not take anything of what you gave them. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah al-Zayyat except Abu al-Jawwab; Muhammad ibn Ghalib is alone in it."
"1327","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hafs narrated to us, he said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands when he opened the prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah except Hafs; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in it."
"1328","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The purification of one of your vessels when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first of them with dust. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ibrahim; Bundar is alone in it."
"1329","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Sufyan Abu Muhammad al-Thaqafi, trustworthy, narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Abi Bakr ibn Umar ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf Abu Damrah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When Umar was stabbed, he was told: O Commander of the Believers, appoint a successor, for if the shepherd of your sheep came to you having left them untended, you would say: You left my sheep without a shepherd? Then what of the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Umar said: If I leave it, one better than me left it, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and if I appoint, one better than me appointed, meaning Abu Bakr. Then he said: Consultation is among these six with whom the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while pleased with them: Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sad. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Asim ibn Abi Bakr, nor from Asim except Abd Allah ibn Sufyan; Ali ibn Muhammad is alone in it."
"1330","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hayyawayh al-Jarjarai Abu Ishaq, trustworthy and reliable, narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Hatim Hibbi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Zayd, from Hakim ibn Kaysan, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who love one another for Allah, mighty and majestic, will be in Allah's shade on a day with no shade but His, upon pulpits of light; people will panic while they do not panic; when Allah, mighty and majestic, intends punishment for the people of the earth, He remembers them and averts the punishment from them by His remembrance of them. No one narrated this hadith from Hakim except Yahya, nor from Yahya except Ali; Hibbi is alone in it."
"1331","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from his father, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Malik ibn Suhar and Mikhnaf ibn Sulaym, from Ali, he said: A weight from the weight of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will settle upon you; woe to you from them, and woe to you for them. No one narrated this hadith from Said except his son Umar, nor from Umar except Sufyan; Ibn Abi al-Wazir is alone in it."
"1332","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah, he said: The one you call Surah al-Tawbah is the Surah of Punishment, and what you recite of it is only a quarter of what we used to recite. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Said except Ibrahim, nor from Ibrahim except al-Numan; Ibn Abi Suwayd is alone in it."
"1333","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah the Exalted will grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection with His left, and the heavens will be in His right, then He will say: I am the King. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1334","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever relieves a distress of a Muslim in this world, Allah, mighty and majestic, will relieve a distress of the Hereafter from him; whoever conceals the fault of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his fault in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah, mighty and majestic, aids the servant as long as the servant aids his brother. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, except al-Hakam."
"1335","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu Dharr was with a small flock of his in Madinah; when he came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu Dharr, and he was silent; he repeated it to him and he was silent, then he said: O Abu Dharr, may your mother be bereaved of you. He said: I am junub. So he called a maidservant for water, she brought it, he screened himself with his mount and bathed, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Clean earth suffices you even if you do not find water for twenty years; when you find it, let it touch your skin. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Hisham, nor from Hisham except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1336","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and we chose him, and it was not a divorce. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1337","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Abu al-Sari, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you come to the prayer, come to it with dignity and calm; pray what you catch and make up what you missed. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1338","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Samurah al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim al-Thaqafi al-Rabi ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Said ibn Jadah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Umm Hani daughter of Abu Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will gather the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection on a single plain; then a caller will call from beneath the Throne: O people of tawhid, Allah, mighty and majestic, has pardoned you. People will rise and cling to one another over the injustices of this world; then a caller will call: O people of tawhid, let each of you pardon the other, and the reward is upon Me. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Hani except with this chain; Abu Asim al-Thaqafi al-Kufi is alone in it."
"1339","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Maymun al-Tabban al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn al-Musayyib said to me: In whose reading do you read? I said: In the reading of Nafi. He said: From whom did Nafi read? I said: Nafi informed us that he read to al-Araj Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, and al-Araj said: I read to Abu Hurayrah, and Abu Hurayrah said: I read to Ubayy ibn Kab, and Ubayy said: I presented the Quran to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Jibril commanded me to present the Quran to you. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ubayd."
"1340","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Harun al-Zaynabi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no man who has a night prayer and sleep overcomes him except Allah, mighty and majestic, records for him the reward of his prayer, and his sleep is charity upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Muslim; Ali is alone in it."
"1341","And with the same chain: from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything and said: No. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Muslim; Ali is alone in it."
"1342","And with the same chain: from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: al-Abbas was captured on the day of Badr, and no shirt fitting him could be found. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Muslim; Ali ibn Harun is alone in it."
"1343","And with the same chain: from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Atiyah al-Qurazi, he said: On the day Sad ibn Muadh judged concerning Banu Qurayzah, I was a boy upon whom the razor had not yet passed, so no judgment was passed upon me. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Muslim; Ali ibn Harun is alone in it."
"1344","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Hour will not come until Isa son of Maryam descends to the earth as a just ruler and an equitable judge; he will break the cross, kill the pig and the ape, abolish the jizyah, and all prostration will be one, to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1345","And with the same chain: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it with stool or urine; face east or west."
"1346","And with the same chain: from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Talhah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not enter a house containing a dog or an image."
"1347","And with the same chain: Rawh narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Gather your livestock and yourselves to you when the sun sets until the darkness of night passes, for Satan comes out at that time; close your doors, extinguish your lamps, for the little mischief-maker may set fire to the household; cover your vessels, even if one of you places a stick across his vessel, for Satan does not open a door nor uncover a covering."
"1348","And with the same chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you should walk in a single sandal, nor eat with his left, nor recline placing one leg over the other, nor wrap himself in the sammah garment. No one narrated these hadiths from Rawh except Muhammad ibn Isa."
"1349","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Shurayh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, concerning His saying: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, he said: When the believer dies he is seated at his grave and asked: Who is your Lord? He says: Allah is my Lord. Then he is asked: Who is your prophet? He says: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. This is repeated to him three times. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yusuf, nor from Yusuf except his son Ibrahim; Shurayh is alone in it."
"1350","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar came, and he said: These two are the masters of the elderly of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. Do not inform them, O Ali. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Ubayd; Ahmad ibn Uthman is alone in it."
"1351","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yazid ibn Yuhannas Abu al-Hasan, from Said ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried Hasan and said: O Allah, I love him, so love him, and love whoever loves him. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ali."
"1352","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man wearing two red garments passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted, but he did not return the greeting. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya except Israil; Ishaq is alone in it."
"1353","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Azraq narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Qasim al-Kindi, from al-Mualla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) holding Ali's hand, saying: This is my ally, and I am his ally. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Wail except al-Mualla."
"1354","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salm ibn Abi al-Dhayyal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn and al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah, mighty and majestic. No one narrated it from Salm except Mutamir."
"1355","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Zurarah ibn Abi al-Halal al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, with us a camel-driver called Anjashah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Anjashah, gently drive the glass vessels."
"1356","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Zurarah ibn Abi al-Halal al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with broth before him containing pumpkin, and he kept seeking it out to eat it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Zurarah except Rawh."
"1357","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten concerning wine: its presser and the one for whom it is pressed, its seller and buyer, its carrier and the one to whom it is carried, its drinker and server, and the eater of its price."
"1358","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour are obscenity and foul speech, severing kinship, distrusting the trustworthy, and trusting the treacherous."
"1359","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No blessing Allah bestows upon a servant for which he says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, except what Allah, mighty and majestic, gives is better than what He took."
"1360","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, whether it falls short or reaches, will have the reward of freeing four persons from the children of Ismail."
"1361","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, will have, for what dust befalls him, musk on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated these hadiths from Shabib except Abu Asim."
"1362","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Salih al-Harithi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, wrote a book two thousand years before creating the heavens and the earth; it is with Him upon the Throne. From that book He sent down two verses with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah, and Satan does not enter a house in which they are recited for three nights. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abbad; Rayhan is alone in it."
"1363","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, concerning His saying: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warner and the guide is a man from Banu Hashim. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sari except al-Muttalib; Uthman is alone in it."
"1364","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Rafi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Tariq, from his father, from Laqit ibn Amir, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about ablution, and he said: When fasting, snuff water gently. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Tariq except Bishr; Safwan is alone in it."
"1365","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Umari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that when he performed ablution he ran his fingers through his beard and between his toes, claiming he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Umar except Muammal."
"1366","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayd Allah Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: My uncle Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from al-Sunabihi, he said: Sad ibn Ubadah narrated to me, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, his heart obeying with it and his tongue humbled by it, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Allah, mighty and majestic, forbids him to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except his son; Ibn Wahb is alone in it."
"1367","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Walid Abu Talib al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, and from Asim, from Zirr, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who delay prayer from its times; if you witness that, pray the prayer at its time and make your prayer with them supererogatory. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz except Abu Bakr."
"1368","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from al-Hasan, from Sasah ibn Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever spends two pairs of his wealth in the path of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him, each inviting him to what is with them: O servant of Allah, this is good; and whoever buries three of his own born children, Allah will admit him to Paradise by His mercy upon them. No one narrated this hadith from Amir except Ibrahim; Khalid is alone in it."
"1369","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Danuqa narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hijazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, enjoin good and forbid evil before you call upon Allah and He does not answer you, and before you seek His forgiveness and He does not forgive you. Enjoining good and forbidding evil does not bring an appointed term nearer; the rabbis among the Jews and the monks among the Christians, when they abandoned enjoining good and forbidding evil, Allah cursed them upon the tongues of His prophets, then affliction encompassed them. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Umari the worshipper except Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Jahdari; Ibn Danuqa is alone in it."
"1370","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas al-Shibami narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: My father had stopped praying with us. I said to him: What is wrong, father, you stopped praying with us? He said: Because you shorten. I said: Then where is the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There are among you the weak, the elderly, and those with needs? He said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Masud say that, and he used to linger in bowing and prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except Abd al-Jabbar; Abu Ahmad is alone in it."
"1371","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Abu Musa's recitation and said: This one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abu Burdah, except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; people narrated it from Malik ibn Mighwal from Ibn Buraydah from his father."
"1372","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in Sad. No one narrated this hadith from Sulaym except Yaqub."
"1373","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Establish prayer at the decline of the sun, he said: When the sun passes its zenith. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Uthman."
"1374","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn al-Walid ibn Abi Khayrah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sight enters, there is no permission. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except al-Walid; his son is alone in it."
"1375","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khirash narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment wrapped around him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except al-Layth and Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"1376","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Husayn Abu Malik al-Saffi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped at Lahy Jamal while fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Bishr. Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah said: He is the brother of Husayn ibn al-Hasan, the companion of Ibn Awn. Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah said: He was called al-Saffi for his keeping to the first row in the Basrah mosque for fifty years."
"1377","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Sulayman al-Taymi, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prostrated at: When the sky splits. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Badal."
"1378","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When we alighted at a stop, we glorified Allah until we loosened the saddles. Shubah said: Glorification with the tongue."
"1379","And with the same chain: Qatadah narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he did not depart from it until he prayed Zuhr. No one narrated these two hadiths from Shubah except Baqiyyah."
"1380","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Mina on the morning of Arafah; when his mount set out with him, bearing a cloak bought for four dirhams, he said: O Allah, make it an accepted Hajj, with no show or repute in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Yazid; Ibn Abi Bazzah is alone in it."
"1381","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall enjoin good and forbid evil, or the worst of you will be set over you, then the best of you will supplicate and not be answered. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Hibban; Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban is alone in it."
"1382","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Jamil ibn al-Hasan al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): a noble and a lowly one; he invoked mercy for the lowly and not for the noble. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you invoked mercy for him but not for me? He said: He remembered Allah so He remembered him, while you forgot Allah so He forgot you. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Abu Hammam."
"1383","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Rustum, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Yahya ibn Said al-Taymi, from al-Mundhir ibn Jarir, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shelters a stray except one astray. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Safwan ibn Rustum; Baqiyyah is alone in it."
"1384","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Muhajir narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, O best of creation. He said: That is my father Ibrahim (peace be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Umar ibn Ubayd; Ibn Muhajir is alone in it."
"1385","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu al-Jawwab."
"1386","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have mercy on those on earth and He in heaven will have mercy on you. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yahya."
"1387","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Hakam ibn Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and: Has there come upon man, and in the Friday prayer: Surah al-Jumuah, and: When the hypocrites come to you. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from al-Hakam, except Muhammad ibn Yazid; Muhammad ibn Hassan is alone in it."
"1388","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Faraj ibn Fudalah, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a man of the Ansar, and I heard him say: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, and honor his abode. Yazid said: Ismail ibn Ayyash came to Baghdad and we heard it from him. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yazid ibn Harun."
"1389","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Sallam Abu al-Musayyib narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih and Salih ibn Abi Salih informed me, from their father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the evening: I seek refuge in all of Allah's perfect words from the evil of what He created, nothing will harm him. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah, from Salih ibn Abi Salih, except Salm."
"1390","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments, with neither shirt nor turban among them. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Isa except al-Muttalib, nor from al-Muttalib except Yahya; Muhammad ibn al-Sakan is alone in it."
"1391","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that he poured water from a skin for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had relieved himself; he performed ablution, washing his face, and went to take his hands out of the jubbah but it was narrow-sleeved, so he brought them out from beneath the jubbah, performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs. Then we came to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who had prayed one rakah, so we prayed one rakah with him and made up the rakah we missed. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman except Abu Dawud."
"1392","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Tasnim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Fadl Kathir ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought moist fresh dates, and said: Where did you get this? They said: We had inferior dates, so we sold two sa for one sa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it to its owner; sell it for money, then buy the dates. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Kathir Abu al-Fadl; Rawh is alone in it."
"1393","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Misar, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Tamim ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn al-As, he said: We were forbidden to visit women whose husbands are absent except with their husbands' permission. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Waki."
"1394","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Humayd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah ibn Sayyar al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Abu Ziyad, meaning Ismail ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about His saying: Allah will bring a people He loves and who love Him. He said: These are a people from Yemen, then from Kindah, then from al-Sakun, then from Tujib. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi except Abu Ziyad, nor from Abu Ziyad except Muawiyah; Abu Humayd is alone in it."
"1395","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah as a close friend. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except al-Fadl."
"1396","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Adi, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn al-Muhallab addressed us in Tabaristan, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people claim a man except he inherits them. al-Haytham said: I narrated it to Isa ibn Musa al-Hashimi, and a man in the gathering said: If only this hadith were from someone other than Yazid. Isa ibn Musa said: Yazid was too noble to lie in hadith."
"1397","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Kab, the silk merchant, narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Nadr ibn Anas, saying: Narrate to me a hadith by which Allah, mighty and majestic, will benefit me. He said: Yes, I shall narrate to you a hadith written to us from Madinah. He said: Anas said: Memorize this, for it is from the treasure of hadith. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on campaign, traveling that day until night. When night came he alighted, the people encamped around him, and he slept with Abu Talhah, the husband of Umm Anas, and so-and-so and so-and-so, four; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pillowed the foreleg of his mount. Then he slept and the four slept beside him. When a portion of the night had passed, they raised their heads and did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his mount, so they went seeking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they met him coming. They said: May Allah make us your ransom, where were you? We feared for you when we did not see you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sleeping where you saw me, then in my sleep I heard a sound like the grinding of a millstone, or a shaking like the shaking of a millstone, so I woke startled in my sleep, rose and went on; Jibril (peace be upon him) met me and said: O Muhammad, Allah, mighty and majestic, sent me to you now to give you the choice: either half your ummah enters Paradise, or intercession on the Day of Resurrection. So I chose intercession for my ummah. The four men said: O Prophet of Allah, make us among those for whom you intercede. He said: It is assured for you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the four came on until ten met him, saying: Where is our Prophet, the Prophet of mercy? He told them what he had told the people, and they said: May Allah make us your ransom, make us among those for whom you intercede on the Day of Resurrection. He said: It is assured for you. They all came to the bulk of the people and called out among them: This is our Prophet, the Prophet of mercy; he told them what he had told the people, and they called out all together: May Allah make us your ransom, make us among those for whom you intercede on the Day of Resurrection. He called out three times: I call Allah to witness, and I call whoever hears to witness, that my intercession is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, mighty and majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Kab except Qurrah ibn Habib; Ali ibn Qurrah is alone in it."
"1398","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: Saad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The passing of my ummah is by spears and plague. They said: Spears we know, but what is plague? He said: Stabs of your enemies among the jinn, and in each is martyrdom. No one narrated this hadith from Saad except Abu Attab."
"1399","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: In this pouch of mine is a hadith; had I narrated it to you, you would have stoned me. Then he said: O Allah, let me not reach sixty. They said: What is sixty? He said: Rule by boys, selling judgment, many police, testimony by acquaintance, treating trust as spoils, charity as a fine, and youths who take the Quran as flutes. Hammad said: And I think he said: And disregard for blood. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammad; Rawh is alone in it."
"1400","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Abu Abbad Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar said: I have been given something of it I know no one was given except that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given it, meaning intercourse. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sari except Yahya."
"1401","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: I never thought any Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) desired this world, until there was revealed concerning us on the day of Uhud: Among you are some who desire this world, and among you are some who desire the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Asbat."
"1402","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yahya ibn Kathir."
"1403","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Kinani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man remains within the scope of his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood."
"1404","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a fortune-teller, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights."
"1405","And from Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night of Muzdalifah, prayed Maghrib and Isha with one iqamah. No one narrated these hadiths from Ubayd Allah except al-Darawardi; Abu Ghassan is alone in them."
"1406","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yunus al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Misar, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Zayd, nor from Zayd except Muammal; Idris is alone in it."
"1407","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from his father, from Sufyan, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, he said: The ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver, its stone of it. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Muafa; his son is alone in it."
"1408","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Murrah, from Fakhitah Umm Hani, that she granted protection to two men, and Ali wanted to kill them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have granted protection to whom Umm Hani granted protection. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Qasim."
"1409","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muslim al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Mikhwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Friday prayer Surah al-Jumuah and: When the hypocrites come to you. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Zaidah, nor from Zaidah except Yahya; Ali ibn Muslim is alone in it."
"1410","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon leaning his back against a wooden post; when people grew many, he said: Build me a minbar. They built him a minbar of only two steps. When he moved from the wood to the minbar, the wood yearned. Anas said: By Allah, I heard the wood yearn with the yearning of a bereaved she-camel, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the minbar to it and embraced it, and it fell silent. al-Hasan said: O servants of Allah, Muslims, the wood yearns for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) longing for him, for his place beside it; are not men who hope to meet him more entitled to long for him? No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Hibban; Yahya ibn Muhammad is alone in it."
"1411","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri and Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah, he said: I heard the recitation and found them close; recite as you were taught, and beware of pedantry and disagreement, for it is but like one of you saying: Come and come hither. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah except Ishaq."
"1412","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Amr al-Hadhda al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people on an intensely hot day and saw a man standing, as if a Bedouin, in the sun. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why do I see you standing? He said: I vowed not to sit until you finish your sermon. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sit; this is not a vow. A vow is only what is intended for the sake of Allah, mighty and majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except his son, nor from his son except Abd Allah ibn Nafi; Muslim ibn Amr is alone in it."
"1413","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Khatmi al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, he said: Aishah daughter of Talhah narrated to me, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: We used to take headbands containing wars and saffron, binding the lower parts of our heads with them at ihram, then entering ihram thus, sweating in them and performing ablution in them until we exited ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Ali ibn Ghurab."
"1414","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Rashid ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu Umamah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj upon a gray mule, led by Khalid ibn al-Walid. No one narrated this hadith from Rashid except Abu Damrah; Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Said is alone in it."
"1415","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Bayan informed me, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim say: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas led us in prayer and stood in the two rakahs; they said: Glory be to Allah. He went on, and when he gave salam he prostrated twice, saying: Thus we did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Baqiyyah; Yahya ibn Uthman is alone in it."
"1416","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lead your people. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find whispering. He struck his hand upon my chest and I never felt it after, and said to me: Lead your people; whoever leads a people, let him lighten, for behind him are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Suwayd."
"1417","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: On the Day of Resurrection you will complete seventy nations; we are the best and the last of them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah."
"1418","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to begin with the prayer before the sermon on Eid. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Muammal."
"1419","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Mustam al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The prayer would be established, and a man would stand speaking to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until some people dozed. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Makhlad."
"1420","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Araj Jabir al-Samti narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Rashid Abu Uthman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Asma daughter of Umays, that a daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and they used to carry men and women equally upon biers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was in Abyssinia, and they are Christians, People of the Book, and they make for a woman a bier with ribs above it, disliking that any part of her form be described; shall I not make for your daughter a bier like it? He said: Make it. She was the first to make a bier used in Islam, for Ruqayyah daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Khalaf; Abu al-Rabi al-Araj is alone in it."
"1421","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Tubba, for he submitted. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muammal; Ibn Abi Bazzah is alone in it."
"1422","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Riyah ibn al-Muthanna, from Ibn Masud, that he used to say every Thursday evening, the night of Friday: The truest speech is the Book of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1423","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah al-Awar, from Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the people of heaven and the people of earth gathered to kill a Muslim man, Allah would hurl them into the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1424","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he was in the house of his aunt Maymunah; water for purification was placed for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He asked: Who placed it? They said: Ibn Abbas. He struck my shoulders, or my chest, and said: O Allah, grant him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1425","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command Bilal to establish the prayer, then turn to a people who heard the call and did not answer, and burn their houses over them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1426","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, she said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking: What is lawful for a man of his wife while she menstruates? He said: What is above the navel. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1427","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I was beside him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1428","And with the same chain: from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: It was acted upon until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away; did any Quran come down after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Meaning the mutah of Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1429","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: An old woman named Mulaykah sent for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he came to us, prayer time arrived, so I went to a mat of ours that had worn, sprinkled it with water, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, with me and two young girls behind him, and the old woman behind us. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1430","And with the same chain: from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they finished tawaf, saying: O Abu Muhammad, what did you do about touching the Corner? He said: I touched and left. He said: You did right. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in it."
"1431","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada narrated to us, he said: I copied from the book of Khalaf ibn Tamim, from Ali ibn Masadah, he said: Abd Allah al-Rumi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that he passed by the market of Madinah, stood over it and said: O people of the market, how incapable you are. They said: What is that, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: That is the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being divided, while you are here, not going to take your share of it! They said: Where is it? He said: In the mosque. They rushed out to the mosque, and Abu Hurayrah waited for them until they returned. He said to them: What is wrong with you? They said: O Abu Hurayrah, we came to the mosque, entered, and saw nothing being divided in it. Abu Hurayrah said to them: Did you see no one in the mosque? They said: Yes, we saw people praying, people reciting Quran, and people discussing the lawful and unlawful. Abu Hurayrah said to them: Woe to you, that is the inheritance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn al-Rumi except Ali ibn Masadah."
"1432","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrating, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This matter will remain firm and lofty until twelve from Quraysh rule. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Khalaf ibn Tamim."
"1433","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Rafiqi narrated to us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched an army or detachment, he summoned its commander, enjoined upon him fear of Allah and good toward the Muslims with him, then said: Fight in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal spoils, nor betray, nor mutilate, nor kill a child or an aged elder. When you come to the people of a fortress or town, do not grant them the covenant of Allah and His Messenger, but grant them your covenants and your fathers' covenants; if you break your covenant and your fathers' covenant, it is better for you than breaking the covenant of Allah and His Messenger. When you besiege the people of a fortress or town, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger, for you do not know whether you hit Allah's judgment concerning them or not; bring them down upon your judgment. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar except al-Ahwas."
"1434","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Rafiqi narrated to us, he said: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the khuffs and the head-cover. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Masruq with this wording except Ammar."
"1435","And Sufyan al-Thawri, his brother Umar ibn Said, Abu Awanah, Abu al-Ahwas, and others narrated it: from Said ibn Masruq, from Amr ibn Maymun and Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed the time for wiping over the khuffs as a day and night for the resident, and three days with their nights for the traveler."
"1436","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the privy, he did not raise his garment until he drew near the ground. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya except Sahl, and the well-known version is from the hadith of Abd al-Salam ibn Harb."
"1437","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: al-Awwam ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while menstruating, and he said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar? I divorced my wife while menstruating, so Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him. He said: Command him to take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her if he wishes before her waiting period. I said: Does she count that divorce? He said: What then? No one narrated this hadith from al-Awwam except Abu Bahr."
"1438","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Sad al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed men who imitate women, and cursed women who imitate men. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Zakariyya; Rawh is alone in it."
"1439","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Muslim al-Hinnai narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Banu Abd al-Dar, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Muawiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding in religion. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Mahak except al-Walid ibn Abd Allah; Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas is alone in it."
"1440","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except Bistam, nor from Bistam except Muhammad ibn Bakr; Muhammad ibn Yahya is alone in it."
"1441","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal and Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a mahram relative is free. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Yahya is alone in it."
"1442","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Abi al-Zard al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The charity of fitr in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only dates, raisins, and barley; it was not wheat. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Ubayd Allah ibn Musa."
"1443","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tumani narrated to us, he said: al-Sakan ibn Ismail al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhda narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Who is Shubrumah? He said: My father. He said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for your father. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhda except al-Sakan ibn Ismail."
"1444","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Hisham al-Qahdhami narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Sakuni al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Mazini, he said: Two Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: Whose life is long and whose deeds are good. The other said: O Messenger of Allah, the practices and laws of Islam have grown many upon me; what do you command me? He said: Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah the Exalted. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Sakuni except al-Walid ibn Hisham."
"1445","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Masud say: Among what we memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that incantations, amulets, and tiwalah are from shirk. His wife said to him: What is tiwalah? He said: Arousal. No one narrated this hadith from Maysarah except Israil."
"1446","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from al-Numan ibn Murrah al-Zuraqi, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Ansar are my trust and confidants; accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari except Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except Bishr ibn Umar."
"1447","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The month of Ramadan entered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This month has entered, a blessed month of Allah, in it a night; whoever is deprived of it is deprived of good, and none is deprived of its good except every deprived one. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal is alone in it."
"1448","And with the same chain: from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever strikes a lash unjustly will be requited on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Zurarah, except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal is alone in it. And Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated it from Imran, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, from Abu Hurayrah."
"1449","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Nafi ibn Abd Allah ibn Ashras al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: I heard Uthman say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a favor to one of the children of Abd al-Muttalib and is not recompensed for it in this world, its recompense is upon me tomorrow when he meets me. This hadith is not narrated from Uthman except with this chain; Yunus ibn Nafi is alone in it."
"1450","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: al-Hudhayl ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Asbagh, from Zadham, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day with two sheets in his hand, looking into them. His Companions said: By Allah, the Prophet of Allah is unlettered; he neither reads nor writes. When he drew near them, he spread the one in his right and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is a book from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, with the names of the people of Paradise, their fathers' names and their tribes, totaled against them, nothing added at its end; your Lord has finished. Then he spread the one in his other hand for the people of the Fire, saying the like of that. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Jahdam is alone in it."
"1451","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Amr ibn Ubayd ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Aqil al-Thaqafi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Hubab ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The prohibition of wine was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when there was not a single grapevine in Makkah, and the vessels were full of unripe and ripe dates, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded regarding them and they were overturned and emptied. No one narrated this hadith from Hubab except Umar."
"1452","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Husayn from al-Shabi, from Imran ibn al-Husayn that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqyah except for the evil eye or a poisonous sting. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Uthman."
"1453","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Uqayl narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Utbah ibn Abdullah Abi al-Umays from Muslim al-Batin, from Amr ibn Maymun who said: I came to Abdullah ibn Masud six times and never heard him narrate anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then one day he narrated a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: or something like this, or close to this, and his face changed color."
"1454","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Abi Husayn from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali ibn Abi Talib that he would go out when Ibn al-Tayyah gave the adhan at the first dawn and say: What an excellent hour for witr this is, interpreting this verse: By the morning when it breathes. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan; al-Mundhir alone narrated it from his father."
"1455","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Mihran narrated to us from Salih al-Ghudani from al-Hasan, from Aws ibn Aws from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever rises on Friday morning, washes and takes a full bath, comes early, walks and does not ride, draws near and does not engage in idle talk, then for every step he has the reward of a righteous deed of fasting and prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Salih, nor from Salih except Humayd; al-Jarudi alone narrated it from his father."
"1456","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Abi al-Zara, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: Whoever goes to a fortuneteller or a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Said."
"1457","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Balj from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If the servants did not sin, Allah would create a creation who would sin, then seek Allah's forgiveness, and He would forgive them, and He is the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Yahya."
"1458","With the same chain: Shubah narrated to us from Abi Hashim al-Rummani from Abi Mijlaz from Qays ibn Abbad, from Abi Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Surat al-Kahf will have a light on the Day of Resurrection from his station to Makkah, and whoever recites ten verses from its end, then the Dajjal emerges, he will not harm him; and whoever performs ablution and says: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, it will be written on a parchment, then placed in a seal, and it will not be broken until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith as marfu from Shubah except Yahya ibn Kathir."
"1459","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from al-Shabi, from Abi Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak who said: A man among us would have two or three names, and he would be called by one of them, and perhaps he would dislike that, so it was revealed: And do not insult one another with nicknames. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Badal and Abu Zayd al-Harawi."
"1460","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me from his father, from Busrah bint Safwan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever touches his penis, or his groin, or his testicles, let him perform ablution as for prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid except Muhammad ibn Bakr."
"1461","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad informed me from his father, from Abdullah ibn Malik Ibn Buhaynah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for the dawn prayer and saw a man praying, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his shoulder and said: Do you pray Fajr four times, or twice? No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Bakr."
"1462","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the day of Ashura and said: That is a day the people of ignorance used to fast, so whoever wishes may fast it and whoever wishes may leave it. No one narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad except Abu Asim."
"1463","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As who said: Breaking the fast while traveling is a concession. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Yahya."
"1464","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Uthman; his son alone narrated it from him."
"1465","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Some dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he began inspecting them. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq except Hammam."
"1466","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Rashid al-Raffa narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas that Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) six children: Abdullah, al-Qasim, Zaynab, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum and Fatimah, and Mariyah bore him Ibrahim. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Shaybah."
"1467","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, he said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us from Abi Ishaq from Harithah ibn Mudarrib who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Allah, clarify for us the matter of wine, so it was revealed: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated, to the end of the verse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Umar and recited this verse to him, but it did not satisfy what Umar wanted, so he said: O Allah, clarify for us the matter of wine, so it was revealed: They ask you about wine and gambling, say: In them is great sin. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Umar and recited it to him, but it did not satisfy what he wanted, so he said: O Allah, clarify for us the matter of wine, so it was revealed: O you who believe, wine, gambling, idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, up to His saying: Will you then desist? He recited it to him, and Umar said: We desist, O Lord. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq from Harithah except Hamzah, nor from Hamzah except Humayd; Muhammad ibn Mamar alone narrated it. And the people narrated it from Abi Ishaq from Abi Maysarah Amr ibn Shurahbil."
"1468","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sabbah Abd al-Ghafur ibn Said al-Ansari narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Hakim, from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophethood and no inheritance. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz except Abu al-Sabbah; al-Shuaythi alone narrated it."
"1469","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Musa ibn Wardan that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah above which there is no rank, so ask Allah the Mighty and Majestic to grant me al-Wasilah over His creation. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah except Ismail."
"1470","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik Abu Bishr al-Tawil narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from al-Mutashammis ibn Muawiyah, the uncle of al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, that he heard Abu Musa al-Ashari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention charity and say: Part of charity is freeing a slave and helping to free him. A man said: Are they not the same? He said: No; freeing him is to set him free yourself, and helping to free him is to assist in it. He said: What if I do not do that? He said: Then a gift of milk or assistance, or kindness to a relative. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Abd al-Malik ibn Musa al-Tawil."
"1471","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Dhira narrated to us, he said: Khaqan ibn Abdullah ibn Ahtam narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the chief of the Arabs? They said: You, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am the chief of the children of Adam, and Ali is the chief of the Arabs. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Khaqan, nor from Khaqan except Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz; Ubaydullah al-Jubayri alone narrated it."
"1472","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Maysarah al-Minqari narrated to us from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever ties a knot then blows into it has practiced magic, and whoever practices magic has committed shirk, and whoever attaches something to himself will be left to it. No one narrated this hadith from Abbad except Abu Dawud."
"1473","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Untuwanah al-Sadi narrated to us from Hamzah Abi Umar, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place he liked to pray Zuhr there before departing. He said: He stopped at a place, and when he wanted to depart he gave the adhan, then prayed while the sun was almost in the middle of the sky. No one narrated this hadith from Untuwanah except Yusuf."
"1474","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from Sulayman al-Amash from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a raid he had fought, and the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were struck by hunger and their provisions ran out, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of what had afflicted them and seeking his permission to slaughter some of their riding animals, and he gave them permission. They went out and passed by Umar, who said: Where have you come from? They told him that they had sought the permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to slaughter some of their camels. He said: Did he give you permission? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you to return with me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They returned with him, and Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you permit them to slaughter their mounts, then what will they ride? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What should I do? I have nothing to give them. Umar said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, command whoever has surplus provisions to bring them, gather them in one place, then supplicate over them, then distribute them among them. He did so: he called them for their surplus provisions, some bringing little and some bringing much; he placed them in one thing, supplicated over them as Allah willed him to supplicate, then divided them among them, and not one of the people remained but filled whatever vessel he had with him, and a surplus remained. At that he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; whoever comes with them on the Day of Resurrection without doubting, Allah will admit him to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl except Ismail ibn Jafar and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim, and no one narrated it from Ismail ibn Jafar except Muhammad ibn Jahdam."
"1475","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Harithah ibn Mudarrib from Abi al-Ubaydayn, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: We used to interpret His saying: And they withhold al-maun as the pot and the bucket and things like that, for people cannot do without them. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq except Yazid."
"1476","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the leather socks and the khimar, meaning the turban. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid except Mualla."
"1477","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the doors opening into the mosque be closed, except the door of Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid except al-Mualla."
"1478","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Asid ibn Zayd al-Jammal narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Surayj from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miqdam except Sharik; Asid ibn Zayd alone narrated it."
"1479","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Usayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a Jew to borrow from him until a time of ease, and he said: What ease? He is one who has neither root nor branch. I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him, and he said: The enemy of Allah has lied; had he given us we would have repaid him. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr; Usayd alone narrated it."
"1480","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated to us from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance in this world, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Rabah except Muhammad; Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"1481","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Mihran al-Dabbagh narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us from Matar al-Warraq from Qatadah, from Anas that a group from Ukl and Uraynah came to Madinah and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of livestock and not people of countryside settlement, and Madinah did not suit us. He ordered them to go out to the charity camels and drink from their milk and urine, so they did and recovered. Then they killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and disbelieved after their Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for them, and they were brought after the day had risen high; he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and they were given no water until they died. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except Dawud, nor from Dawud except Dawud ibn Mihran; Ibrahim ibn Rashid alone narrated it."
"1482","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Quran was sent down on the Night of Decree in the month of Ramadan to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was sent down in portions. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran; Muhammad ibn Bilal alone narrated it."
"1483","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us from his father from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abi Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer sees a private fault of his brother and covers it for him except that Allah admits him to Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Mualla alone narrated it."
"1484","With the same chain: from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abi al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sees a private fault of his brother and covers it for him, Allah admits him to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid except Mualla."
"1485","With the same chain: from Abd al-Hamid from his father from Abdullah ibn Kharijah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing in prostration and blowing on food. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid except Mualla."
"1486","With the same chain: from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep until he recited Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, al-Sajdah, and Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion."
"1487","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Dinar from Abi al-Sha'tha, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man unable to perform Hajj; may I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Tell me, if your father owed a debt and you paid it, would it not suffice for him? No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Zakariyya."
"1488","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hoarding food in Makkah is deviation from the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ibn Muhaysin; Abdullah ibn al-Muammal alone narrated it."
"1489","With the same chain: Abdullah ibn Muammal narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and performed his tahnik. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abdullah ibn Muammal."
"1490","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam Abu Amr al-Madani narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the market of Dhu al-Majaz before he emigrated, going around among the people saying: O people, Allah the Mighty and Majestic commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him; and behind him a man saying: O people, this man commands you to abandon the religion of your fathers. I said: Who is this? They said: His uncle Abu Lahab. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Said; Abd al-Samad alone narrated it."
"1491","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Yala ibn Hakim from Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man's debtor becomes bankrupt and he finds his goods intact with him, he has more right to them than the other creditors. No one narrated this hadith from Yala except Jarir; Wahb alone narrated it."
"1492","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awf al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us from al-Awzai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you stand for prayer, come to it with tranquility upon you; whatever you catch, pray it, and whatever you miss, complete it."
"1493","With the same chain: al-Awzai narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: The most beloved of My servants to Me are those quickest to break the fast. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Awzai except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"1494","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us from al-Ajlah and Habib ibn Hassan from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah at sunset and did not pray Maghrib until he reached Sarif, which is nine miles away. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Abd al-Rahim; Abdullah ibn Umar alone narrated it."
"1495","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Ashath ibn Sawwar from Abi al-Zubayr from al-Saib ibn Yazid from Abdullah ibn al-Sadi who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: We send you on one of the people's affairs, yet you refuse the wages; what carries you to that? I said: I have no need of it. He said: Do not do so; take it, for I intended what you intended, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give me something and I would say: O Messenger of Allah, give it to one poorer than me; then once he gave me some wealth and I said the same, wanting not to take it, and he said: Take it; keep it as wealth or give it in charity, for when Allah gives you wealth while you are not asking for it, take it, and what is turned away from you, do not pursue it with your soul. No one narrated this hadith from Abi al-Zubayr except Ashath; Abd al-Rahim alone narrated it."
"1496","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Munib narrated to us from his father that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, and the wives of the Ansar, and their offspring. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Munib except Muhammad ibn Khalid."
"1497","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Dinar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Abi Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you say when you go to your bed? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: When you go to your bed in a state of purity, place your right hand as a pillow, then say: O Allah, I submit myself to You, turn my face to You, entrust my back to You, in fear and hope of You; there is no refuge nor escape from You except to You; I believe in Your revealed Book and Your sent Messenger; for no servant says them in his night then dies except that he dies upon the fitrah. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari."
"1498","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Masadah narrated to us from Riyah ibn Ubaydah, from Itban ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah sincerely with both, and prays the five prayers, Allah forbids his face to the Fire."
"1499","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Masadah narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah sincerely with both, and prays, fasts, gives zakat and performs Hajj to the House, Allah forbids him to the Fire. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ali ibn Masadah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Humran."
"1500","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Abbas Abd al-Malik al-Shami narrated to me, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Ubadah ibn Nusayy who said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five degrees. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Abd al-Malik al-Shami al-Kattani; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"1501","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father, from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Attab ibn Asid to Makkah and said: Convey to them four traits: that two conditions in a sale are not valid, nor a sale combined with a loan, nor profit on what is not guaranteed. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar except Muhammad ibn Sulayman."
"1502","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-As al-Qurashi al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us from al-Wadin ibn Ata from Yazid ibn Marthad, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam at the end of the even part of witr and at the end of the witr itself. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin except Sadaqah; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"1503","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik from Furat ibn Thalabah al-Hizzani from Abi Muslim al-Khawlani; Abu Muslim said: Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah testified before me that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No people gather remembering Allah the Mighty and Majestic except that the angels surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Muslim except Furat, nor from Furat except Abd al-Karim; Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud alone narrated it."
"1504","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abi al-Anbas from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For me to give my ring in charity is dearer to me than to dedicate a thousand dirhams to the Kabah."
"1505","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father, he said: Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last Isha prayer until nearly a third of the night had gone, then he came out to the mosque and found few people in it, so he became angry, then said: I had intended to command men, when the prayer is established, to stay behind to the houses of those who do not attend the prayer and burn their houses over them. And he said: If a man invited people to food they would come to it, yet prayer is called for and they do not come to it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"1506","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father from al-Hakam from Abi Muhammad from Muslim ibn Subayh from Masruq ibn al-Ajda, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: Whatever I have forgotten from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I have not forgotten that he would give salam to his right and to his left at the end of the prayer, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the side of his face was visible to us. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud; his son alone narrated it from him. And Abu Muhammad from whom al-Hakam narrated is al-Amash."
"1507","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to me from his father Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, he said: al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to me from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza who said: A man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Ammar ibn Yasir went out on a raid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ammar had a wet dream and began rolling in the dust. When he returned he told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to Ammar: You rolled as a donkey rolls; it would have sufficed you, and he motioned with his hands to the ground, to place them like this. Salamah said: To strike the earth with your hands, then wipe your face and forearms, and pray. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"1508","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My grandfather narrated to me from his father from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abi Umamah al-Bahili who said: Had I not heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except once or twice or three or four or five or six times, I would not have narrated it. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution well, sin leaves his hearing, sight, hands and feet. Abu Zabyah al-Himsi, sitting with us, said: Did you not hear Amr ibn Abasah narrate this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: And I heard him say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps in purity remembering Allah and does not turn in an hour of the night asking Allah the Mighty and Majestic for something of this world or the Hereafter except that Allah the Mighty and Majestic gives it to him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"1509","And from al-Hakam from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding His saying: And they will not disobey you in what is right. Umm Atiyyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stipulated upon us that we would not wail."
"1510","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Abi Mashar Ziyad ibn Kulayb from Ibrahim al-Nakhai from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The believer dies with sweat on the forehead. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Yazid, nor from Yazid except Mualla."
"1511","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqawwim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Ammar ibn Yasir and his family while they were being tortured for the sake of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and said: Rejoice, family of Yasir; your appointment is Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abi al-Zubayr except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Muslim; Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it."
"1512","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu Ghassan al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Hafs al-Muzani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Aishah say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until many mines appear, inhabited only by the worst of people. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman except Hafs; Yahya alone narrated it."
"1513","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Musa al-Tawil narrated to us from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal from Asim al-Ahwal from Abdullah ibn Sarjis who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. I said: Did he seek forgiveness for you? He said: Yes, and for you, and he recited this verse: And seek forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and women. No one narrated this hadith from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal al-Qadi except Abd al-Malik; Hilal alone narrated it."
"1514","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas who said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm informed me from Abbad ibn Tamim that Abu Bashir al-Ansari informed him: He was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a messenger calling out: No string necklace shall remain on a camel's neck except that it be cut. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Muhammad."
"1515","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from al-Amash from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Abi Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with four statements, saying: Allah the Mighty and Majestic does not sleep, nor is it fitting for Him to sleep; He lowers the balance and raises it; the deeds of the day are presented to Him before the night, and the deeds of the night before the day; His veil is light, and had He removed it, the splendor of His face would have burned everything His sight reached. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash from Abdullah ibn Murrah except Sufyan; Muammal alone narrated it, and the people narrated it from al-Amash from Amr ibn Murrah."
"1516","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ismail al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Hinnai narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abdullah ibn Malik Ibn Buhaynah that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand from two rakahs, forgetting to sit, and continue his standing, then prostrate two prostrations after finishing his prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ali except Harun."
"1517","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Kathir ibn Faid narrated to us from his father from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through one of the lanes of Madinah and saw a dead black man thrown in the road; he asked some of those there about him, saying: Whose slave is this? He said: A slave of such-and-such family. He said: Did you see him pray? They said: We would sometimes see him pray and sometimes not pray. He said: Stand, wash him and shroud him. They stood, washed and shrouded him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed over him. When he said takbir he said: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, his companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we heard you each time you said takbir say: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah; why did you say: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah? He said: The angels almost came between me and him from the multitude of those praying over him. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Kathir ibn Faid; his son alone narrated it. Abu al-Qasim said: The explanation of this hadith is that his masters would sometimes witness him praying, and sometimes he would pray where they did not see him, so they belittled him for that; had he abandoned any prayer without praying it, he would have been a disbeliever, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between the servant and disbelief is abandoning prayer."
"1518","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind who said: I heard Nafi narrate, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make his brother stand from his seat and sit in his place."
"1519","With the same chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of a third."
"1520","With the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque, took something and scraped it off, and said: Let none of you spit toward his qiblah, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic faces him; rather let him spit to his left or under his foot. No one narrated these hadiths from Abdullah ibn Said except Ghundar."
"1521","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Makhshi ibn Muawiyah al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father, from Aishah that Sawdah gave her day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Aishah. No one narrated this hadith from Makhshi except Muhammad ibn Abbad."
"1522","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Shubah from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling wala and giving it as a gift. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad except Ibrahim; his son alone narrated it."
"1523","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi Salih narrated to us that he heard Nafi ibn Jubayr narrate, from his father who said: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Hijr, al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As passed by, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to my ummah from what is in the loins of this man. This hadith is not narrated from Jubayr except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Khalaf alone narrated it."
"1524","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us from Said ibn Bashir from Matar al-Warraq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father, from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Fajr except two rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except Said; Rawwad alone narrated it."
"1525","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah from Mujahid, from Qays ibn al-Saib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was my partner in the pre-Islamic period, and he was the best of partners, neither quarreling nor disputing. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Muhammad ibn Muslim; Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"1526","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father, he said: Ibrahim al-Nakhai and Sulayman ibn Qays narrated, from Abdullah ibn Masud that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the parable of provision like a wall with a door: what is around the door is easy, and what is around the wall is rough and rugged; whoever comes to it from its door attains all of it safely, and whoever comes to it from its wall falls into roughness and ruggedness, until when he reaches it he has only the provision Allah the Mighty and Majestic facilitated for him. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except his son; Yahya alone narrated it."
"1527","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ubadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us from Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feeding food and speaking good words admit you to Paradise; O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, feed food and speak good words. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Munkadir except Umar; Abdullah ibn Dawud alone narrated it."
"1528","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, he said: Aidh ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting and looked at a hole facing him, and said: If hardship came until it entered this hole, ease would come until it expelled it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Indeed with hardship comes ease; indeed with hardship comes ease."
"1529","With the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, exchange gifts, for a gift removes rancor and bequeaths love; by Allah, were a trotter gifted to me I would accept it, and were I invited to a foreleg I would answer. No one narrated these two hadiths from Anas except Aidh."
"1530","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us from Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with those you love. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs except Muhammad ibn Musa al-Yamami; Umar ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"1531","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Zaidah narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from fatigue in travel and gloom upon return. O Allah, fold the earth for us and ease travel for us; O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. When it was time to return he would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord; and when it was the day he reached his family he would say: A return, a return to our Lord, a return leaving no sin upon us. No one narrated this hadith from Zaidah except Yaqub. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym from Simak."
"1532","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Thawr ibn Yazid from Maslamah ibn Abi Ata from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam, naqir and muzaffat vessels. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Abu Asim."
"1533","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bistam al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: al-Mualla ibn al-Fadl al-Qushayri narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. Aishah said: I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, do you fear while you are the Messenger of Allah? He said: O Aishah, the hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; whomever He wills He turns from misguidance to guidance, and from guidance to misguidance. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak except Mualla; Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"1534","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab Jafar ibn Hayyan narrated to us from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding al-Hasan ibn Ali: This son of mine is a chief, and I hope that Allah the Mighty and Majestic will reconcile two parties of Muslims through him. No one narrated this hadith from Abi al-Ashhab except al-Ansari."
"1535","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us from Umar ibn Amir from Qatadah from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Amir except Salim ibn Nuh."
"1536","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Artah ibn Ashath Abu Hatim narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father, from Aishah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Each of you is a shepherd and responsible. No one narrated this hadith from Artah Abi Hatim except al-Jubayri."
"1537","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that a man accused his wife and denied her child in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them both and they invoked mutual curses as Allah the Mighty and Majestic stated, then he assigned the child to the woman and separated the two who invoked curses. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except al-Qasim; Muqaddam alone narrated it."
"1538","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Abi al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn Asid who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the drop settles in the womb and forty nights pass over it, the angel comes to it and says: O Lord, male or female? The Lord the Mighty and Majestic dictates and the angel writes. He says: What is his provision? What is his lifespan? The Lord dictates and the angel writes. And he says: Wretched or blessed? The Lord dictates and the angel writes. Then he folds the scroll."
"1539","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Hafsah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command the faraah from sheep, one from every fifty sheep. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim; Muqaddam alone narrated them."
"1540","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Bishr narrated to us from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Ismail ibn Said ibn Urwah from Jundub ibn Abdullah who said: I was with Ali on the day of al-Nahr, and he said: Seek the Mukhdaj. He was sought but not found, so Ali said: By Allah, I have neither lied nor been lied to. Then Ali stood going among the slain until he reached a pile in a low spot of the ground among the slain, and said: Stir these. They were stirred, and there was the Mukhdaj, with on his forearm something like a woman's breast. He said takbir and said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Yunus; Salm alone narrated it."
"1541","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Sawadah ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Qurrah al-Muzani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abbas would be asked about exchange and give fatwa permitting it, so Abu Said al-Khudri spoke stern words. Ibn Abbas said: Who is speaking? They said: Abu Said. He said: I did not think a man would confront me while knowing my kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Said said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it and declare it unlawful. Thereafter when Ibn Abbas was asked about it he would say: We met one more knowledgeable than us, he informed us, and we desisted. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah except Sawadah; Yaqub alone narrated it."
"1542","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us from Khusayf from Mujahid, from Kab ibn Ujrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kab ibn Ujrah, do the lice of your head harm you? I said: Yes. He said: Then shave, and slaughter a sheep, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Muhammad, and Khusayf did not place Ibn Abi Layla between Mujahid and Kab."
"1543","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us from Khulayd ibn Dalaj from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Khosrow and Caesar and to every tyrant, calling them to Allah the Mighty and Majestic, when this verse was revealed to him: And this Quran has been revealed to me that I may warn you thereby and whomever it reaches. No one narrated this hadith from Khulayd except Rawwad."
"1544","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh from his father, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wipe over the leather socks when traveling for three days and their nights, and when resident for a day and a night. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Said."
"1545","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Raja ibn al-Murajja narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us from Thumamah, from Anas who said: Four compiled the Quran in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ubayy ibn Kab, Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu Zayd and Muadh ibn Jabal. Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah said: Abu Zayd is Sad ibn Ubayd al-Qari who was at al-Qadisiyyah, and he is the father of Umayr ibn Sad. No one narrated this hadith from al-Husayn except his son Ali."
"1546","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution twice each time. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr except Muhammad."
"1547","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father, from Aishah who said: I would comb the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Man."
"1548","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Jamil ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas who said: The caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced that the qiblah had been turned to the Sacred House, while the imam had prayed two rakahs; so they turned around and prayed the remaining two rakahs toward the Sacred House. No one narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Jamil; Zayd alone narrated it."
"1549","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Arubah from Ayyub from Nafi, from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Abd al-Ala."
"1550","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group from Banu Amir, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we find stray camels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stray of a Muslim is the fuel of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Ibn Mahdi."
"1551","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father, from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow does not avert anything of the decree; rather it is extracted thereby from the miser. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except al-Hasan ibn Habib."
"1552","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ashkab narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to us from Abi Raja, from Umar ibn al-Khattab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out stoning. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Raja except Khalid ibn Muhammad; Abu Nuaym alone narrated it."
"1553","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail from Umarah ibn Asim al-Anbari who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat vessels."
"1554","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us from Sharik from Jabir from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic is entrusted with something He returns it, and Luqman, peace be upon him, said to his son: Entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts and the seals of your deeds. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Jabir, nor from Jabir except Sharik; al-Fadl alone narrated it."
"1555","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Mikhwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis al-Nakhai from Kumayl ibn Ziyad who said: I heard Ali say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will recite the Quran whose knowledge will not pass their throats. Among them is a man with a deformed hand, or a hand with a small deformity, with hairs at its ends. When the day of al-Nahrawan came, Ali said: Seek him. They did not find him, then they followed and found him. Ali said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Kuhayl except Abd al-Rahman, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Qays; Mikhwal alone narrated it."
"1556","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we hear things from you that we wish to preserve; shall we write them? He said: Yes. I said: What about what occurs in anger and pleasure? He said: Yes, for I do not say in anger or pleasure except the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abu Kudaynah, nor from Abi Kudaynah except Muhammad; Ahmad ibn Uthman alone narrated it."
"1557","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Habhabi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal and Ibn Jurayj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a loan combined with a sale, two conditions in a sale, selling what has not been taken possession of, and profiting from what is not guaranteed. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hammam; Amr alone narrated it."
"1558","With the same chain: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Matar al-Warraq from Salim, from his father who said: I traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar, and I never saw them add to two rakahs, two rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except Hammam; Amr alone narrated it."
"1559","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik al-Zibaqi Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit remembering Allah the Mighty and Majestic except that a caller from heaven calls to them: Rise forgiven, for your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun ibn Ajlan except Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik."
"1560","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Abi Nadrah, from Abi Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr, O people of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Aban ibn Yazid."
"1561","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah narrated to us from his father, from Abi Said al-Khudri regarding this verse: O you who believe, when you contract a debt, up to His saying: But if one of you trusts another: He said: This verse abrogated what came before it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah except Muhammad ibn Marwan."
"1562","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn al-Musayyab al-Bajali al-Qadi narrated to us from al-Shabi, from al-Ashath ibn Qays who said: I once bought my oath for seventy thousand, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever severs a Muslim's right by an oath meets Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him."
"1563","With the same chain: Isa narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Four matters of the son of Adam are decreed: his form, his character, his lifespan and his provision."
"1564","With the same chain: Isa narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abi Said al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying when a Bedouin passed with his milking animal, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him but he did not understand. Umar called to him: O Bedouin, behind you. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who spoke? They said: Umar. He said: He has no understanding of this. No one narrated these hadiths from Isa except Safwan."
"1565","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three are together, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that grieves him; and a woman should not describe another woman to her husband as if he were looking at her; and whoever severs a Muslim man's wealth by his oath meets Allah the Exalted while He is angry with him. No one narrated this hadith from Ararah except Rayhan; Yahya ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"1566","Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Muqri al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from al-Shabi, from Utbah ibn Farqad who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, the devils are chained, and a caller calls: O seeker of good, come forward; O seeker of evil, desist, until the month ends. No one narrated this hadith from Ata from al-Shabi except Abd al-Salam; Abu Bilal alone narrated it."
"1567","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Shaybah al-Minqari narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abi Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not created a disease except that He has created its cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it, except death, which is al-sam. No one narrated this hadith from Ata from Abi Said except Shabib; and Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated it from Ata from Abi Hurayrah, and Talhah ibn Amr narrated it from Ata from Ibn Abbas."
"1568","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab al-Bajali narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer and senses impurity or doubt, let him not leave until he hears a sound or smells an odor. No one narrated it from Abi Kudaynah except Abu Bilal."
"1569","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us from Abi Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Jahm al-Qurashi, from Abdullah ibn Umar from Umar regarding wiping over the leather socks; Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it, so we did it. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Bakr al-Nahshali except Abu Bilal."
"1570","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umarah narrated to us from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim from Hakim ibn Umayr, from Aishah who said: Neither little nor much barley bread would remain on the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Hakim except his son al-Ahwas; Bishr alone narrated it."
"1571","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah al-Sunabihi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wakes fasting then has a wet dream, is cupped, or is overcome by vomiting, there is no makeup upon him; but whoever deliberately vomits, makeup is upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam from al-Sunabihi except Muhammad ibn Aban."
"1572","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi al-Asadi narrated to us from Abi Husayn from Abi Salih al-Hanafi, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while part of my garment was over him, and I was menstruating. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Husayn except Qays and Zaidah."
"1573","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Fadl al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Nafi al-Ijli narrated to us from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman from Ibrahim from Alqamah, from Ammar ibn Yasir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me, and I said: O Jibril, tell me of the virtues of Umar in heaven. Jibril said: Had I told you of the virtues of Umar for as long as Nuh remained among his people, a thousand years less fifty, the virtues of Umar would not be exhausted; and Umar is one good deed among the good deeds of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Ismail; al-Walid alone narrated it."
"1574","Ahmad ibn Isa ibn al-Sukayn al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: Qatadah ibn al-Fudayl ibn Qatadah al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: How do you perform ablution? He said: You ask me how I perform ablution and do not ask me how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution? I saw him perform ablution three times each. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Qatadah; al-Zubayr alone narrated it."
"1575","Ahmad ibn Hamdun al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghuzayl ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Afif ibn Salim al-Bajali narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri from Layth from Tawus, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take condiment even with water. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Afif; Ghuzayl alone narrated it."
"1576","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Afif ibn Salim narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafs al-Ansari from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How excellent are those who clean between their teeth from my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Raqabah except Muhammad, nor from Muhammad except Afif; Muhammad alone narrated it."
"1577","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us from Hisham ibn Sad from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar, from Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about cheese? He said: Cut with the knife, mention the name of Allah, and eat. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Hisham, nor from Hisham except al-Muafa."
"1578","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri from Mansur from Mujahid from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: All flies are in the Fire except bees; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing them and burning food. Sufyan said: It is likely to be in enemy land. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Qasim; Muhammad ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"1579","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuzai narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Salman al-Farisi entered upon Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was reclining on a pillow, and he threw it to him. Salman said: Allah is Greatest; Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Umar said: Narrate to us, O Abu Abdullah. He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a pillow, and he threw it to me, saying: O Salman, no Muslim enters upon his brother and throws him a pillow honoring him except that Allah forgives him. This hadith is not narrated from Salman except with this chain; Imran alone narrated it."
"1580","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ulathah from al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah from Abi Umayr, from Salman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls are grouped troops; those of them that recognize one another unite, and those that do not recognize one another differ."
"1581","With the same chain: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When speech becomes manifest, deeds are hoarded, tongues differ, hearts hate one another, and every kinsman severs his kinship, at that Allah curses them, deafens them and blinds their sight. These two hadiths are not narrated from Salman except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ammar alone narrated them."
"1582","Ahmad ibn Hamdun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: A man from the people said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, when a man pays the zakat of his wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pays the zakat of his wealth, its evil has departed from him. No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Umar; Muhammad ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"1583","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abd al-Samad al-Asadi al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us from Israil from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Israil, nor from Israil except al-Qasim; Salih alone narrated it."
"1584","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Afif ibn Salim narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Utbah from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar that a man from Abyssinia came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have been favored over us in color and prophethood. Tell me, if I believe as you believe and do as you do, shall I be with you in Paradise? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, he has thereby a covenant with Allah; and whoever says: Glory be to Allah, Allah writes for him a hundred thousand good deeds. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we perish after this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, a man will come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds that, were they placed on a mountain, would weigh it down; then a blessing from the blessings of Allah will stand and almost consume all of that, were it not for what Allah bestows of His mercy. Then it was revealed: Has there come upon man a time of the age, up to His saying: And when you look there you see bliss and great dominion. The Abyssinian said: O Messenger of Allah, shall my eye see in Paradise what your eye sees? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. The Abyssinian wept until his soul departed. Ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lowering him into his grave. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ayyub; Afif alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"1585","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyub, Ibn Awn, Hisham and Salamah ibn Alqamah from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke during prayer forgetfully, then continued upon what he had prayed. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Mualla."
"1586","Ahmad ibn Isa Abu al-Harish al-Kilabi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Abi al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while two disputants were disputing before him, and he said: Judge between them. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; you are more entitled to that. He said: Judge between them. I said: Upon what? He said: Exert yourself; if you are right, you have ten good deeds, and if you err, you have one good deed. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Hafs; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan alone narrated it. And it is not narrated from Uqbah except with this chain."
"1587","Ahmad ibn Muhammad Abu Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Mukhariq narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abi Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: Hajj is in well-known months: Shawwal, Dhul Qadah and Dhul Hijjah. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Husayn; Muhammad ibn Thawab alone narrated it."
"1588","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Masqalah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr al-Nahri narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Ansari from his father, from his grandfather Aslam al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed me in charge of the captives of Banu Qurayzah, and I would look at the private part of the boy; if I saw that he had grown pubic hair I struck his neck, and if I did not see that he had grown it I placed him among the spoils of the Muslims. This hadith is not narrated from Aslam al-Ansari except with this chain; al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"1589","Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ishaq al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Asfar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Humayd al-Kufi, the son-in-law of Ubaydullah ibn Musa, narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man ibn Thalabah narrated to us from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah from Ibrahim al-Nakhai from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid and Fahd ibn Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Masud that he threw the jamrah from the belly of the valley and said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Aban except al-Qasim, nor from al-Qasim except Ahmad ibn Humayd; Ibn al-Asfar alone narrated it."
"1590","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Asfar narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Adam al-Akbar narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us from Aban ibn Thalabah from Fudayl ibn Amr from Ibrahim from Abidah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite to me. I said: Shall I recite to you when it was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than me. I began and recited Surat al-Nisa until I reached: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you against these as a witness. His eyes, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, filled with tears, so I stopped. He said to me: Ask, you will be given. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl except Aban, nor from Aban except al-Qasim, nor from al-Qasim except Bishr; Ibn al-Asfar alone narrated it."
"1591","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Mukram al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Farahij narrate, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Abu Ghassan; Ali alone narrated it."
"1592","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us from Abi Hazim from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: A crescent and a crescent would pass us, and no fire would be lit in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said to her: O aunt, then on what did you live? She said: On the two black things: water and dates. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ghassan except Ali."
"1593","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us from al-Amash from Abi Sufyan, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three days before his death saying: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"1594","With the same chain: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced in his prostration, and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."
"1595","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"1596","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones, and I was forbidden to tuck up a garment or hair. No one narrated these hadiths from Abu Ja'far except Ali."
"1597","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari from Nafi' from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd from Hafsah bint Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for three days, except over her husband. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari except Yahya ibn Zakariyya."
"1598","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people with the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection will be an unjust ruler. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abu Hafs."
"1599","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Ghalib from Abu Umamah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghalib except Hammad."
"1600","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Ali from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he commanded the woman with prolonged vaginal bleeding to perform ablution for every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi, who is Abdullah ibn Ali, except Abu Yusuf."
"1601","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us from al-Ajlah al-Kindi from Abdullah ibn Dhakwan from al-A'raj, who said: Abdullah ibn Buhaynah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and did not sit after the first two rak'ahs, so he prostrated two prostrations of forgetfulness, then gave the salutation. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Abu Yusuf."
"1602","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, magnifying Allah over them nine times, then seven times, then four times, until he joined Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Abu Yusuf."
"1603","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us from al-A'mash from al-Sha'bi from Fatimah bint Qays, who said: My husband divorced me three times, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have no maintenance and no lodging. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Yusuf and Hafs."
"1604","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf al-San'ani narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Yazid."
"1605","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us from Abu Hanifah from Asim ibn Kulayb from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited some people of the Ansar at their house, so they slaughtered a sheep for him and prepared food from it for him; he took some meat to eat it, and chewed it for a while without being able to swallow it, and said: What is the matter with this meat? They said: It is the sheep of so-and-so; we slaughtered it until its owner comes, so that we may compensate him with its meat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed it to the captives."
"1606","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abdullah narrated to us from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir from Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you doubts and does not know how much he has prayed, let him strive to be certain until he is sure, then complete upon his certainty, then prostrate two prostrations of forgetfulness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Abdullah except Abu Yusuf."
"1607","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us from Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal from Ibn Buraydah from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my nation is eighty rows of them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sa'd except Abu Yusuf."
"1608","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf narrated to us from Abu Hanifah from Hammad from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Abu Hanifah and Sufyan al-Thawri; Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham alone narrated it from Sufyan, and Abu Yusuf alone narrated it from Abu Hanifah."
"1609","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umayr narrated to us from Makhul from Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rulers, and supplicate for their righteousness, for their righteousness is righteousness for you."
"1610","And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither dust in the nostrils of a servant in the path of Allah nor the smoke of Hell gather together. No one narrated these two hadiths from Makhul except Musa; Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ta'i alone narrated them."
"1611","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us from Simmak ibn Harb from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times, and he used to sit with his Companions reciting poetry to one another, and they would sometimes recall matters of the pre-Islamic age, and they would laugh, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would smile with them."
"1612","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us from his father from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May Allah have mercy on one who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for many a one conveyed to has more understanding than the hearer."
"1613","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two bargains in one bargain are not lawful."
"1614","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us from his father from Qabus ibn Mukhariq from his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think of a man who meets me in an empty land wanting my wealth? He said: Remind him of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he does not remember? He said: Then seek help against him from the Muslims around you. He said: What if there is no one around me? He said: Then seek help against him from the ruler. He said: What if the ruler is far from me? He said: Then fight for your wealth until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter, or you protect your wealth."
"1615","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us from his father from Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah from his grandmother Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me on the day of the conquest of Makkah while I was fasting, so I brought him a cup of milk, and he drank and said: Drink. I said: I am fasting. He said: A fast of makeup? I said: No. He said: Then drink. So I drank. No one narrated these hadiths from Ibn Simmak, whose name is Sa'id, except Abd al-Malik."
"1616","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Unays ibn Sawwar al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills to create a person, when the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers; then on the seventh day Allah brings to him every line of ancestry between him and Adam. Then he recited: In whatever form He willed, He assembled you. This hadith is not narrated from Malik except with this chain; Unays alone narrated it."
"1617","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shabab narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, he said: A man of ours called Muqatil narrated to us from Qutbah ibn Qatadah al-Sadusi, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, extend your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you for myself and for my daughter al-Huwaysilah; and if I had lied against Allah I would have deceived you. He said: And Khalid ibn al-Walid attacked us with his cavalry, so we said: We are Muslims, so he left us. And we raided al-Ubullah with him, and divided it, and filled our hands. This hadith is not narrated from Qutbah except with this chain; Awn alone narrated it."
"1618","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shabab narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Kahmas narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best people of the East are Abd al-Qays. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Awn."
"1619","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shabab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Salih ibn Khawwat ibn Salih ibn Khawwat ibn Jubayr al-Ansari narrated to me from his father from his grandfather Khawwat ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, a small amount of it is unlawful."
"1620","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Asim ibn Damrah from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four before Friday and four after it, making the salutation at the end of them in one rak'ah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Husayn, and no one narrated it from Husayn except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sahmi."
"1621","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Salih from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah from Ali, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, if a matter befalls us in which there is no clarification, neither command nor prohibition, what do you command us? He said: Consult the jurists and the worshippers, and do not carry out in it a private opinion. No one narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn Salih except Nuh."
"1622","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of your lifetimes compared to the nations that have passed is like what is between the Asr prayer and sunset; and the likeness of you and the Jews and Christians is like a man who employed workers and said: Who will work for me until midday for a qirat each? So the Jews worked until midday for a qirat each, and the Christians worked from midday until the Asr prayer for a qirat each. Then he said: Who will work for me from the Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats each? Verily, for you is the reward twice over. So the Jews and Christians became angry and said: We did more work and have less reward? He said: Have I wronged you of your right in anything? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty; I give it to whom I will. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Wahhab except Abu Abd al-Rahim; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone narrated it."
"1623","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Raja al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id Abu Ghifar, the seller of carpets, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Sha'tha Jabir ibn Zayd say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him from exchanging currency for currency; I have met one more knowledgeable of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than me, and he informed me that it is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghifar except Isa."
"1624","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Muslim from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the sacrifice for a newborn: Whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice on his behalf, let him do so. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Isma'il."
"1625","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: We recited to Ma'qil ibn Ubaydillah from Maymun ibn Mihran from Ibn Umar, who said: The Magians were mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: They let their mustaches grow long and shave their beards, so differ from them. And Ibn Umar used to trim his mustache, cutting it as one cuts a sheep. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun except Ma'qil."
"1626","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: We recited to Ma'qil from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: I divorced my wife at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating, so Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned Abdullah's wife to him; then when she became pure, he said: Divorce if you wish, or keep her."
"1627","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us from Amr ibn al-Harith from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, who said: We were eating dates on a shield, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us, having come from relieving himself, so we said: Come, so he came forward and ate dates with us, and did not touch water. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Amr; Musa alone narrated it."
"1628","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihsan narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Makhul from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two sects of this nation will not attain my intercession: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah."
"1629","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'allal ibn Nufayl narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Rashid from al-Zuhri from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty years old."
"1630","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse, and his right side was scraped, so he led us in prayer sitting, and we lined up with him sitting; then when we finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is only appointed to be followed, so when he magnifies Allah, magnify, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You belongs praise; and when he prays standing, pray standing, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting, all of you. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq except Musa."
"1631","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man al-Farra al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us from al-Rabi' ibn Abi Salih from Majza'ah ibn Zahir from Salamah ibn al-Akwa', that his uncle struck a man of the polytheists, killing him and wounding himself, and he began saying: I have killed myself. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: He has two rewards. No one narrated this hadith from al-Rabi' ibn Abi Salih except Abdullah ibn Khirash; Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man alone narrated it."
"1632","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yazid al-Sayyari narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Suhaym, the freedman of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, narrated to us from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"1633","And from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to his Companions: Learn Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing, and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot overcome it."
"1634","And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculine women."
"1635","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Maghazili al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Abu Sufyan from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ablution is the key to prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Muhammad ibn Himyar; al-Maghazili alone narrated it."
"1636","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Maghazili narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us from Ja'far ibn Muhammad from his father from Safwan ibn Umayyah, that he lent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weapons, eighty coats of mail, and Safwan said to him: Is it a guaranteed loan or seizure? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Rather, a guaranteed loan. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Abu Damrah; al-Maghazili alone narrated it."
"1637","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Sa'id al-Marwazi narrated to us at Tarsus, he said: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Ubaydillah ibn Umar from al-Qasim from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Ali."
"1638","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Sa'id al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah ibn Asid, I think he raised it, who said: The Beast will emerge from the most sacred of mosques. While they are sitting, the earth will rumble, and while they are like that, it will split open. Ibn Uyaynah said: It will emerge when the imam hastens from Muzdalifah, and the early pilgrim was only appointed to inform the people that the Beast has not emerged. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Sufyan; Hamzah ibn Sa'id alone narrated it."
"1639","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us from Hisham from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed, would place his right hand under his right cheek and say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Musa; Sa'id alone narrated it."
"1640","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa Isa ibn Yunus al-Tarsusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I have prepared for My righteous servants what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"1641","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not seen the like of Paradise, whose seeker sleeps; and I have not seen the like of Hell, whose fleer sleeps. No one narrated these two hadiths from Qatadah except Hammam; Muhammad ibn Mus'ab alone narrated them."
"1642","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hafs narrated to us from Abu al-Ahwas from Khalid ibn Alqamah from Abd Khayr, who said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went first, and Abu Bakr prayed, and Umar was third, then tribulation struck us as Allah willed. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid except Abu al-Ahwas, and no one from Abu al-Ahwas except Mu'awiyah; Muhammad ibn Musaffa alone narrated it."
"1643","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad from Husayn ibn Abdullah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Hashim, coldness will befall you after me, so seek help against it through the most delicate of people."
"1644","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us from al-Rabi' ibn Anas from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever remembers Allah and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah until his tears reach the ground, Allah will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1645","And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends blessings upon me, his blessing reaches me, and I bless him, and ten good deeds are written for him besides that. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Ja'far except Muhammad ibn Sulayman."
"1646","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah al-Mazini narrated to us from Qays ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath ibn Qays from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears an oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him; He will punish him or forgive him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Sa'id ibn Hubayrah al-Basri."
"1647","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Antaki narrated to us, and Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Farra narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri from Husayn ibn Abdullah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, who said: The polytheists used to depart from Arafah before sunset, and would not depart from Muzdalifah until the sun declined, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opposed them: he departed from Arafah after sunset when the fasting person breaks fast, then departed from Muzdalifah before sunrise. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad."
"1648","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr al-Ansari, who said: I handed the banner to Abdullah ibn Rawahah, and he was struck, so he handed it to Thabit ibn Aqram al-Ansari, who handed it to Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: Why did you hand it to me? He said: You know fighting better than me. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Abu Ishaq."
"1649","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib ibn Abi al-Ishrin narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Qilabah from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, Exalted, has prescribed fairness; and when one of you wants to slaughter, let him sharpen his blade and comfort his slaughtered animal. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Ibn Abi al-Ishrin; Hisham alone narrated it."
"1650","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Zayd ibn Muhammad from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for us nor for our freedmen. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except his brother Umar, and no one from Umar except Isma'il; Hisham alone narrated it."
"1651","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ufayr ibn Ma'dan narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is red, light-skinned, bulky, with coarse features, as if the hair of his head were branches of a tree, as if his eye were the morning star; I likened him to Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan of Khuza'ah. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ufayr; al-Walid alone narrated it."
"1652","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Hisham ibn Urwah from Muhammad ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating with his three fingers: the thumb, the one next to it, and the middle; then I saw him licking his three fingers before wiping them, licking the middle, then the one next to it, then the thumb. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid."
"1653","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Bashir from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, that the Negus married the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Umm Habibah, and gave her dowry on his behalf from his wealth, two hundred dinars. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id, and no one from Sa'id except Sufyan; Marwan alone narrated it."
"1654","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Manbiji narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us from Habib ibn Salih al-Ta'i, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit narrated to me from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, he said: Say: O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah to you, and know that the return is to Paradise or to Hell: eternity without death, residence without departure, in bodies that do not die. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Sa'id."
"1655","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas from Abdullah and Muhammad, the sons of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from their father from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, that they said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and his wives and his offspring, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim; and bless Muhammad and his wives and his offspring, as You blessed Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. No one narrated this hadith from Malik, from Abdullah and Muhammad the sons of Abu Bakr, except Isa; and people narrated it from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr alone."
"1656","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah Mus'ab ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Wa'il ibn Dawud from al-Bahiyy from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed a man of Quraysh as a captive on the day of Badr, then said: No Qurashi shall be killed as a captive after this day except a man who kills Uthman ibn Affan, so kill him; and if you do not, you will be killed like the slaughter of sheep. None narrates it except Mus'ab, and it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"1657","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Shu'bah from Ya'la ibn Ata from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no servant who sends blessings upon me except that the angels bless him as long as he sends blessings upon me, so let him do much or little. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah, from Ya'la, except Isa; and people narrated it from Shu'bah from Asim ibn Ubaydillah."
"1658","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Ibn Awn from al-Sha'bi from Jarir ibn Abdullah, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, that Mu'adh had a dispute with a man, so they brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he placed the oath upon one of them; the other said: O Messenger of Allah, you let him swear over my land, so he takes it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he swears falsely, then he said a severe statement. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Isa."
"1659","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'dan al-Salamsini narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats the flesh of his brother in this world will have it brought near to him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: Eat it alive as you ate it dead. So he will eat it, grimacing and screaming. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except Muhammad ibn Salamah."
"1660","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to us from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari from Nafi', that he entered with his cousin upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and asked him about exchanging currency; so Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Gold for gold, like for like, and silver for silver, like for like, with no excess between them. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Ubaydillah."
"1661","Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Mansur ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us from Dawud al-Warraq from Sa'id ibn Hakim from his father from his grandfather Mu'awiyah ibn Haydah al-Qushayri, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I was brought to him, he said: I have asked Allah to help me with a year of drought that wears you out, and with terror He places in your hearts. So he said with his hands together: I have sworn thus and thus that I will not believe in you nor follow you. The year of drought kept wearing me out, and terror kept being placed in my heart until I stood before you. By Allah who sent you, did He send you with what you say? He said: Yes. He said: And did He command you with what you command us? He said: Yes. He said: What do you say about our women? He said: They are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish, and feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear, and do not strike them, and do not starve them. He said: May one of us look at the private part of his brother when we gather? He said: No. He said: What when we are apart? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined one of his thighs over the other and said: Allah is more deserving that you be modest before Him. He said: And I heard him say: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with servants upon them, and the first thing that speaks of a person is his hand and his thigh. Sufyan said: And their servants: that their tongues are seized."
"1662","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la al-Sami narrated to us from Hisham ibn Hassan from Jarir ibn Hazim from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: Umar addressed us at al-Jabiyah; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in my standing place today among you, and said: Be good to my Companions, then those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man testifies to testimony without being asked for it, and until he swears an oath without being asked for it; so whoever wants the middle of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the one, and he is farther from two; and let none of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them; and whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abd al-A'la."
"1663","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed me, he said: My father narrated to me from Amir al-Ahwal from Makhul from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz from Abu Mahdhurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the call to prayer, saying: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then return and say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham al-Dastuwai except his son Mu'adh; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1664","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us from Sufyan from Ja'far ibn Muhammad from his father from Jabir, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, he entered the mosque, touched the Stone, then went to his right, trotting three circuits and walking four, then came to the Station and said: And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer; then he prayed two rak'ahs, with the Station between him and the House, then he came to the House after the Corner, touched the Stone, then went out to al-Safa. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Yahya."
"1665","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a mat of palm leaves and prostrate upon it. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except al-Attaf; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"1666","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdah ibn Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Bayan ibn Bishr, he said: I heard Humran say: I heard Uthman say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abdullah ibn Humran."
"1667","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Burd, the brother of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral then prays over it will have a qirat of reward, and whoever walks with the funeral until it is buried will have two qirats of reward, and the qirat is like Uhud. It is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Abthar alone narrated it."
"1668","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar informed me, he said: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; and: Say, O disbelievers; and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"1669","Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Musa informed me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us from al-A'mash from Zubayd and Talhah from Dharr from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; and: Say, O disbelievers; and: Say, He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ja'far except al-Dashtaki, and no one narrated it from al-A'mash except Abu Ja'far and Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah."
"1670","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us from Ubaydillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab from Amrah from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Six I have cursed, and every answered prophet has: the one who adds to the Book of Allah, and the denier of Allah's decree, and the violator of Allah's sacred bounds, and the violator of what Allah has made sacred of my progeny, and the abandoner of the Sunnah. No one narrated this hadith, with a connected chain, from Ubaydillah except Ibn Abi al-Mawal."
"1671","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father from Mughirah from his father from al-Aswad, he said: I asked A'ishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch his wife while fasting? She said: Yes, but he had the most control of you over his desire. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mu'tamir."
"1672","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Ma'bad from Ibn Abbas, who said: I only knew the end of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayer by the takbir."
"1673","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilabah from Abu Shu'ayb from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was holding my hand on the morning of the eighteenth night past of Ramadan, he glanced and saw a man being cupped, and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken fast. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abd al-A'la."
"1674","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf narrated to us from Ata from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped have broken fast. No one narrated this hadith from Rabah except Abu Ahmad."
"1675","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from Muhammad ibn Juhadah from Abu Salih from Ubayd ibn Umayr from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dyed yellow garments and silk brocade, and gold rings, and that bordered with silk; then he said: And know that I am to you among the sincere advisers. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Zayd, and no one from Zayd except Abu Abd al-Rahim; Muhammad alone narrated it."
"1676","Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Bistami narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, he said: Simmak ibn Harb narrated to us from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a man dozed on his mount, so a man took an arrow from his quiver, and the man woke and was frightened; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to frighten a Muslim. It is not narrated from al-Nu'man except with this chain, and we know none who narrated it from Simmak except Anbasah, and none narrated it except al-Husayn ibn Isa."
"1677","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Zayyat narrated to us, he said: Awf al-A'rabi narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted horse meat and forbade the meat of domestic donkeys. Awf al-A'rabi narrated no supported hadith from Amr except this hadith, and none narrated it except Ali ibn al-Husayn from Ibrahim; and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it, inserting between Amr ibn Dinar and Jabir: Muhammad ibn Ali."
"1678","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Nasr informed me, he said: Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Bara, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: What is your name? He said: Nu'm. He said: You are Abdullah. None narrated it from Abu Ishaq except Abd al-Kabir."
"1679","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: Jabir ibn Marzuq narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Umari from Abu Tuwalah al-Ansari from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin and knows that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, if He wills punishes him and if He wills forgives him, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Tuwalah except Abdullah, and no one from Abdullah except Jabir; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"1680","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed me, he said: I said to Abu Qurrah: Did Musa ibn Uqbah mention from Amr ibn Abi Amr from Anas ibn Malik, that a man entered the mosque seeking a lost item, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it? So he affirmed it and said: Yes. None narrated it from Musa except Abu Qurrah."
"1681","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani informed me, he said: Abu Usamah Zayd ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Burqan informed me from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq from Ibn Jurayj from Ata from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the grave of a woman after she was buried. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Habib, and no one from Habib except Ja'far; Zayd ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"1682","Ahmad informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Rabi' ibn Anas say: I recited the Quran to Abu al-Aliyah, and Abu al-Aliyah recited to Ubayy ibn Ka'b. He said: And Ubayy said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I was commanded to recite the Quran to you. I said: Was I mentioned there? He said: Yes. He said: So Ubayy wept; he said: And I do not know whether out of longing or fear. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aliyah except al-Rabi'."
"1683","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Zayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi informed me, he said: Sayf ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, he said: Sarrar ibn Mujashshir narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi' and Salim from Ibn Umar, that Ghaylan ibn Salamah had ten wives, so he embraced Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to choose four. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Sarrar; Sayf alone narrated it."
"1684","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Maymun from Abu al-Ahwas from Masruq from A'ishah, who said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What an evil servant of Allah and brother of the tribe; then he came in to him afterwards, and I saw him turn to him with his face, as if he held a status with him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ahwas except Ibrahim; Shu'bah alone narrated it."
"1685","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Ya'fur, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about wiping over the leather socks? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ya'fur except Abu Awanah, and none narrated it from Abu Awanah except Qutaybah and Nu'aym ibn al-Haytham."
"1686","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mu'afa Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani informed me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahim from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from Malik ibn Anas from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: May Allah have mercy on a servant who had against him a wrong toward his brother, in honor or wealth or status, so he seeks his pardon before it is taken, when he will have neither dinar nor dirham; if he has good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds, and if he has no good deeds, some of his companion's sins will be placed upon his sins. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Abu Abd al-Rahim; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone narrated it."
"1687","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Hassan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut the hand for a quarter dinar. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs except Ja'far."
"1688","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from his father from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the slave are his food and his clothing, and he is not burdened with work except what he can bear. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibrahim and al-Nu'man ibn Abd al-Salam al-Taymi."
"1689","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs informed me, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Shu'bah from Hakim ibn Jubayr from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from his father from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who asks for something while having what suffices him, except that it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches or marks or a blemish on his face. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, and what suffices him? He said: Fifty dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Ibrahim and Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan; and none narrated it from Yahya except Musaddad."
"1690","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Yazid Amr ibn Yazid informed me, he said: Sayf ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prostration is upon seven limbs: the two hands, the two feet, the two knees, and the forehead."
"1691","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Raising the hands: when you see the House, and on al-Safa and al-Marwah, and at Arafah, and at Muzdalifah, and when stoning the pillars, and when the prayer is commenced. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ata except Warqa, and no one from Warqa except Sayf; Abu Yazid alone narrated it."
"1692","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Qudamah ibn Shihab narrated to us from Burd ibn Sinan from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that Gabriel came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and taught him the prayer times: Gabriel stepped forward, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he prayed Zuhr when the sun declined, and he came to him when the shadow was like his figure, and did as he had done; Gabriel stepped forward, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him, and the people behind the Messenger of Allah, and prayed Asr; then he came to him when the sun set, Gabriel stepped forward, with the Messenger of Allah behind him and the people behind the Messenger of Allah, and prayed Maghrib; then he came to him when the twilight disappeared, Gabriel stepped forward with the Messenger of Allah behind him and the people behind the Messenger of Allah, and prayed Isha; then he came to him when dawn broke, Gabriel stepped forward with the Messenger of Allah behind him and the people behind the Messenger of Allah, and prayed Fajr; then he came to him the second day when a man's shadow was like his figure, and did as he had done the day before, and prayed Zuhr; then he came to him when a man's shadow was twice his figure, and did as he had done the day before, and prayed Asr; then he came to him when the sun set, and did as he had done the day before, and prayed Maghrib; then he came to him when the twilight disappeared, and did as he had done the day before, and prayed Isha; then he said: What is between these two prayers is the time."
"1693","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq: Did Ibn Jurayj mention from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day wearing a striped cloak, and said to a man of his Companions: Give me your cloak and take mine? He said: O Messenger of Allah, your cloak is better than mine. He said: Yes, but in it is a red thread, so I feared I would look at it and it would tempt me? And he affirmed it? He said: Yes. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Sarjis except with this chain; Ibn Jurayj alone narrated it."
"1694","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Mansur informed me, he said: Mubashshir ibn Abdullah informed me, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us from Ya'la ibn Muslim from Jabir ibn Zayd from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah were emigrants because they abandoned the polytheists; and there were emigrants among the Ansar, because Madinah was a land of polytheism, so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of al-Aqabah. No one narrated this hadith from Ya'la except Sufyan, and no one from Sufyan except Mubashshir."
"1695","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali informed me, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed me from Thawr ibn Yazid from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, who said: We used to say at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except al-Walid; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1696","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Yazid Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Ubaydillah, and he was trustworthy, narrated to us from Salamah ibn al-Ayyar from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Dimashqi from al-Zuhri from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Do you see the sun on a day with no clouds? We said: Yes; and do you see the moon on a night with no clouds? We said: Yes. He said: Then you will see your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, so much so that one of you will converse privately with his Lord in intimate discourse, saying: My servant, do you remember such-and-such sin? And he will say: My Lord, did You not forgive me? And He will say: By My forgiveness you have reached this. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sa'id, and no one from Sa'id except Salamah, and no one from Salamah except Sayf; Abu Yazid alone narrated it."
"1697","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali informed me, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Ata from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not make his wife enter the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table over which wine is served. It is said: Ata, from whom Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated this hadith, is Ata ibn al-Sa'ib. And none narrated this hadith from him except Hisham, and none from Hisham except his son; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1698","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us from Umar ibn Amir from Qatadah from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah from Umm Salamah, who said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the blanket, I menstruated, so I slipped away to take my menstrual clothes; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. She said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting, and they would bathe from one vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar, and no one from Umar except Salim; Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"1699","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Kinani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from the nephew of Ibn Shihab from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ibn Khallad informed me that his father heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you relieves himself, let him wipe three times. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except his nephew, and no one from the nephew of al-Zuhri except Abu Ghassan; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi alone narrated it."
"1700","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Harb al-Marwazi informed me, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us from his father from Yazid al-Nahwi from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and they took booty, and among them was a man who said: I am not of them; I fell in love with a woman and followed her, so let me look at her one glance, then do with me as you wish. They looked, and there was a tall, dark woman, and he said to her: Accept Islam, Hubaysh, before life runs out. She said: Yes, may I be sacrificed for you. So they brought him forward and struck his neck. The woman came, stood over him, gasped once or twice, then died. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Was there not among you a merciful man? This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Harb alone narrated it."
"1701","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qutaybah informed me, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me from Salim from Ibn Umar, who said: I was a young unmarried man, and I used to spend the night in the mosque, and when one of them saw a dream he would bring it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to interpret it. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except al-Walid; Amr alone narrated it."
"1702","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Adhrami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Harami narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you follows a funeral, let him not sit until it is placed on the ground. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Qasim; al-Adhrami alone narrated it."
"1703","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi informed me, he said: al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Sufyan from Jabalah ibn Suhaym from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garments out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Ashja'i; Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"1704","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq informed me, he said: I heard Musa ibn Uqbah mention from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr mentioning that he asked A'ishah about kissing for the fasting person? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting, then she laughed. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Abu Qurrah; Ishaq alone narrated it."
"1705","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed me, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti informed me, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas from his father, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw me in poor appearance and said: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, Allah has given me all kinds of wealth. He said: If you have wealth, let it be seen upon you. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il except Muhammad ibn Yazid and Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani, the two Wasitis."
"1706","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed me, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed me, he said: My father narrated to me from Qatadah from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will question every shepherd about what he was entrusted with, whether he preserved it or neglected it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh alone narrated it."
"1707","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah informed me, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: An accepted pilgrimage has no reward but Paradise, and one Umrah to another is expiation for what is between them. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il except Humayd; al-Hasan alone narrated it."
"1708","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim informed me, he said: Shurayh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us from his father from Abu Ishaq from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wa'il ibn Hujr al-Qayl, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strike with his right upon his left in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq, and no one from Yusuf except Ibrahim; Shurayh alone narrated it."
"1709","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to me, he said: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir, who said: A thief was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Cut him. So he was cut; then he was brought a second time, and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Cut him. Then he was brought a third time, and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Cut him. Then he was brought a fourth time, and he said: Kill him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he only stole. He said: Cut him. Then he was brought a fifth time, and he said: Kill him. Jabir said: So we took him to the camel pen, then we attacked him; he lay on his back, and we stoned him and killed him, then we threw him into a well, then we threw stones over him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Mus'ab."
"1710","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh informed me, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi informed me, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us from Ubaydillah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the one for whom the Throne shook, and for whom the gates of heaven were opened, and seventy thousand angels witnessed him; he was squeezed a squeezing, then relief was given to him. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Ibn Idris."
"1711","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs informed me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman informed me from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from Anas, who said: Nothing after women was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than horses. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id except Ibrahim."
"1712","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me from Musa ibn Uqbah from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been permitted to speak of an angel of the Throne-bearers: between his earlobe and his shoulder is a journey of four hundred years. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Ibrahim."
"1713","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only branded the eyes of those Uranis because they branded the eyes of the shepherds. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except Yazid; Yahya alone narrated it."
"1714","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Harb al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Yazid al-Nahwi from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar wine."
"1715","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rafi' al-Naysaburi informed me, he said: Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Nusayr al-Ta'i narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, raising the hadith, who said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in truth, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he acts by it and teaches it."
"1716","And with the same chain, from Dawud al-Ta'i from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Jarir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"1717","And from Dawud al-Ta'i from al-A'mash from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: The evil deed is one, or I forgive; and the good deed is ten or more. And whoever comes to Me with sins filling the earth, not associating anything with Me, I will make it forgiveness for him; and whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"1718","And with the same chain, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was saying: They are the greatest losers, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. I said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Those with the most wealth, except one who says with wealth thus and thus; and by Him in whose hand is my soul, no man dies leaving camels or cattle or sheep without paying their zakat, except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection as great and fat as can be, goring him with their horns and trampling him with their hooves; whenever the last of them passes, the first returns, until judgment is passed among people."
"1719","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash from Umarah ibn Umayr from Abu Ma'mar from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders and say: Straighten, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ; let those of understanding and reason be next to me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."
"1720","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the truthful, the believed, narrated to us: The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty nights, then he is a clot like that, then he is a lump like that, then the angel comes to him and says: My Lord, male or female? Wretched or happy? And what is the provision? And what is the term? So your Lord decrees, and the angel writes."
"1721","And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: We were with Hudhayfah in the mosque, and a man from the gates of Kindah entered and began praying a prayer without completing its bowing and prostration, so Hudhayfah said: For how long have you prayed this prayer? He said: For forty years. He said: You have not prayed for forty years, and if you died you would die upon other than the nature of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1722","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash from Ibrahim ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, he said: Umar came to the Stone, touched it, and said: I know you are a stone; were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss you, I would not kiss you."
"1723","And from al-A'mash from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i from Hammam ibn al-Harith from Jarir, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."
"1724","And from al-A'mash from Ibrahim al-Taymi from his father, that temporary marriage was mentioned to Abu Dharr, so he said: It was only a concession for us, the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1725","And from al-A'mash from Thumamah ibn Uqbah from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man of the People of the Book said: O Abu al-Qasim, do you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink? He said: Yes; by Him in whose hand is my soul, one of them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating and drinking and intercourse and desire. He said: One who eats will need to relieve himself? He said: The need of one of them is sweat that comes out like the scent of musk, and his belly shrinks."
"1726","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sayf narrated to us from Dawud al-Ta'i from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding the other, for that grieves him."
"1727","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, concerning Allah's saying: And spend in the path of Allah and do not cast yourselves into destruction, he said: It was revealed concerning spending."
"1728","And with the same chain, from Shaqiq from al-Sabiyy ibn Ma'bad, that he entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together; he mentioned that to Umar, who said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1729","And from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Masruq from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither dinar nor dirham, nor sheep, nor camel, nor did he bequeath."
"1730","And from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every prophet has an answered supplication, and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation."
"1731","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the weak and the elderly and the one in need."
"1732","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the softest in hearts and tenderest in hearts. Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni; and harshness and hardness of heart are among the loud-voiced owners of camels toward the east, in Rabi'ah and Mudar."
"1733","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with an iron, his iron will be in his hand, stabbing his belly with it in Hell, abiding eternally therein forever; and whoever throws himself from a mountain will keep falling in the fire of Hell, abiding eternally therein forever; and whoever sips poison will keep sipping it in the fire of Hell, abiding eternally therein forever."
"1734","And with the same chain, from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced, and let him not spread his forearms as a dog spreads."
"1735","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"1736","And from Jabir from Abu Sa'id, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, wrapped in it. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Ta'i except Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam."
"1737","Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani informed me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahim from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from Talhah ibn Musarrif from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Bedouins of Uraynah came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Madinah disagreed with them, until their colors turned yellow and their bellies swelled; so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to some milch camels of his, and commanded them to drink from their milk and urine, so they drank until they recovered; then they killed his shepherd and drove off the camels; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, and they were brought, and he cut their hands and feet on opposite sides and branded their eyes. The Commander of the Believers Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan said to Anas, while he was narrating this hadith: For disbelief or for sin? He said: For disbelief. He said: This verse was only revealed after he cut their hands and feet and branded their eyes: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger, the verse."
"1738","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashshar al-Nasa'i narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih informed me, he said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us from his brother Abdullah ibn Ubaydah from Ammar ibn Yasir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The lawful is clear, and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters; whoever avoids them is more pious for his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into them is about to fall into major sins, like one grazing beside a sanctuary, about to fall into it; and every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary is His bounds. It is not narrated from Ammar except with this chain."
"1739","Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Farqad al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Ubaydillah ibn Umar from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made sacred upon my tongue what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah; then he came to Banu Harithah and said: You have gone out of the sanctuary; then he looked and said: No, rather you are within it."
"1740","And with the same chain, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs: eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley. No one narrated these two hadiths from Musa except Abu Qurrah."
"1741","1738 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'sa'ah narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of disbelief is toward the east, and pride and arrogance are among the people of camels and wool, and tranquility and dignity are among the people of sheep. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri from al-A'raj except al-Zubaydi, and Yazid ibn Yusuf al-San'ani, a Damascene."
"1742","1739 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf al-San'ani narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Nafi' from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."
"1743","1740 - And with the same chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted Khaybar (land) on (the condition of) half (the produce)."
"1744","1741 - And from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and none after Asr until the sun sets."
"1745","1742 - Ahmad ibn Musa al-Jawhari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited with them in Maghrib: (Those who disbelieve and bar from the way of Allah). No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Abu Mu'awiyah; al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"1746","1743 - Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Ja'd al-Washsha' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Qurashi narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not inform you of your men in Paradise? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Prophet is in Paradise, and the truthful one is in Paradise, and the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn child is in Paradise, and the man who visits his brother in a distant part of the town, visiting him only for the sake of Allah, is in Paradise. Shall I not inform you of your women in Paradise? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every loving, child-bearing woman who, when she becomes angry or is wronged, says: Here is my hand in your hand, I will not sleep until you are pleased. No one narrated it from Abu Hazim except this Ibrahim, and it is not narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"1747","1744 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Anas ibn Malik who said: Umm Ayman gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a bird between two loaves. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Do you have anything? So she brought him the bird, and he raised his hands and said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird. Then Ali came, and I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is busy, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had only just entered and taken a little of the bird. Then he raised his hand and said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me from this bird. Then Ali came, and voices rose between me and him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Admit whoever it is. So he entered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ally, O Lord, three times, and he ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they finished. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abd al-Razzaq; Salamah alone narrated it."
"1748","1745 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Zayd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: I testify that my father narrated to me from his father from his grandfather Husayn ibn Ali who said: The Ansar came to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Aqabah, and he said: Stand, O Ali, and take their pledge. He said: Upon what shall I take their pledge, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon (the condition) that Allah is obeyed and not disobeyed, and that they protect the Messenger of Allah and his household and his offspring as they protect themselves and their offspring. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Husayn; Abdullah ibn Marwan alone narrated it."
"1749","1746 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim al-Janbi narrated to us from al-Ajlah from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Habbah ibn Juwayn al-Urani from Ali that he said: O Allah, You know that no one from this ummah worshipped You after its Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before me, and I worshipped You six years before anyone of this ummah worshipped You. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ajlah except Amr."
"1750","1747 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar ibn Burdah narrated to me, he said: Wahb ibn Munabbih said: My brother Hammam said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as he waits for the next one, and the angels continue to invoke blessings upon one of you as long as he remains in his mosque: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, as long as he does not break his ablution. A man from Hadramawt said: What is that breaking of ablution, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth: passing wind, loudly or silently. No one narrated this hadith from Wahb except Abd al-Rahman."
"1751","1748 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Musa al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Sulayman ibn Musa from Makhul that he entered upon Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard him mention that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, benefit me by what You have taught me, and teach me what will benefit me. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Sulayman, nor from Sulayman except Umarah, nor from Umarah except Isma'il; al-Mu'afa al-Zuhri al-Himsi alone narrated it."
"1752","1749 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mutawakkil ibn Muhammad ibn Sawrah narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Atiyyah narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in running water. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Harith."
"1753","1750 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Yazid ibn Sinan from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from Amr ibn Murrah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, these pebbles which are thrown every year, we think they decrease. He said: Whatever is accepted of them is lifted up, and were it not for that you would have seen them like mountains. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Zayd; Yazid ibn Sinan alone narrated it."
"1754","1751 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn al-Akhil narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us from Janab ibn Nistas from Sharik from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: When (And if you fear that you cannot do justice to the orphans) was revealed, they feared regarding women similarly that they would not give (their due), so (Marry such women as seem good to you) was revealed up to His saying: (That is nearer to prevent you from doing injustice). No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Janab; Mubashshir alone narrated it."
"1755","1752 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from my grandfather Aban ibn Sulayman from his father Sulayman from Qabath ibn Ashyam al-Laythi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A promise is a gift. This hadith is not narrated from Qabath except with this chain; Asbagh alone narrated it."
"1756","1753 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir from Sulayman ibn Musa from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani from Aws ibn Aws who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches the Friday prayer, then washes and performs full ablution, then goes early and arrives at the beginning, then draws near to the imam and listens attentively, will have for every step the reward of a year's deeds, its standing (in prayer) and its fasting. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nu'man except Muhammad."
"1757","1754 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Ayyub al-Sukkari al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit occasionally, and love will increase. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Walid."
"1758","1755 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah who said: Umar said: We were commanded to bathe on Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Azhar; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"1759","1756 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Fazari narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which deeds are more beloved to Allah than the ten days. It was said: Not even jihad in the way of Allah? He said: No, except a man who goes out with his life and wealth and then returns with nothing of that."
"1760","1757 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Jabir who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that we would not flee, and we did not pledge him upon death. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Isa; Sa'id alone narrated it."
"1761","1758 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, and Malik ibn Anas from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every religion has a character, and the character of this religion is modesty. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Isa; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"1762","1759 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn al-Akhil narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us from Janab ibn Nistas from Sharik from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: (And they intended what they could not attain), he said: A man called al-Aswad intended to kill the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Janab; Mubashshir alone narrated it."
"1763","1760 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us from Mughirah from Abu Ishaq from Asim ibn Damrah from Ali who said: Witr is not obligatory, but it is the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Abu Ishaq; Ubayd alone narrated it."
"1764","1761 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shabur al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a resting place of musk like the resting places of your animals in this world. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Abd al-Hamid; Muhammad ibn Shabur alone narrated it."
"1765","1762 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Mutawakkil ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sawrah narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Atiyyah narrated to us from al-Awza'i from Qurrah from al-Zuhri from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was screened by a curtain in which there was an image, so he tore it down and said: The most severely punished people on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one included Qurrah in the chain of this hadith between al-Awza'i and al-Zuhri except al-Harith."
"1766","1763 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Ibn Thawban from Ata' from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No newborn is born except five verses of the Opening of the Book are written in the parting of his head."
"1767","1764 - And from Ibn Thawban from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani from his father from Ibn Abbas that Umm Kulthum came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the husband of Fatimah is better than my husband. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent for a while, then said: Your husband is loved by Allah and His Messenger, and he loves Allah and His Messenger, and I add for you: if you enter Paradise and see his station, you will not see anyone of my companions above him in station."
"1768","1765 - And from Ibn Thawban from Humayd ibn Hani' from Abbas ibn Julayd al-Hajari from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the servant who sins? He said: He is pardoned seventy times every day."
"1769","1766 - And from Ibn Thawban from Layth from Makhul from Qaza'ah ibn Yahya from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus? He said: Do you create him? Do you provide for him? Leave him in his place."
"1770","1767 - And from Ibn Thawban from Sa'id ibn Ayyub from Ka'b ibn Alqamah from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the five prayers and said: Whoever guards them, they will be for him a light, a proof, and a salvation on the Day of Resurrection."
"1771","1768 - And from Ibn Thawban from Nafi' from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day of Ramadan in attentiveness and silence, a house will be built for him in Paradise of green peridot or red ruby. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except al-Walid ibn al-Walid al-Qalanisi."
"1772","1769 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Razi al-Isfadhani narrated to us in Baghdad, he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Razi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak from Jarir ibn Shurahbil from Ibn Qattah, freedman of Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me of three which I will never abandon until I meet him: fasting three days of every month, the two rak'ahs of Duha, and Witr before sleeping. No one narrates this hadith from Sulayman ibn Qattah, freedman of al-Husayn ibn Ali, except Jarir ibn Shurahbil, nor from Jarir except al-Jarrah; Ali ibn Abi Bakr alone narrated it. The name of Ibn Qattah is Sulayman; he narrates from Ibn Abbas, and Musa ibn Abi A'ishah and others narrated from him."
"1773","1770 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra' narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us from Umar ibn Ibrahim from Qatadah from al-Hasan from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will remain upon the natural disposition as long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars interlink. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar; Abbad alone narrated it, and no one narrated it from Abbad except Ibrahim ibn Musa, his son Awwam ibn Abbad, and Muhammad ibn Adam al-Marwazi."
"1774","1771 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Habib ibn Hassan from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Hujr ibn Adi al-Kindi from Ali who said: A'ishah bint Abi Bakr knew that the people of al-Nahrawan are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"1775","1772 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from al-Sha'bi from Masruq from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not disappoint a servant who stands in the middle of the night and opens Surah al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and excellent is the treasure of a man: al-Baqarah and Al Imran. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Layth, nor from Layth except Fudayl; Bishr alone narrated it."
"1776","1773 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until we would say: He does not break his fast, and he would break his fast until we would say: He does not fast, and most of his fasting was in Sha'ban. No one narrated this hadith from Umar except Ali."
"1777","1774 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Isa ibn al-Dahhak al-Kindi from al-A'mash from Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Masruq from Umar ibn al-Khattab that he said: Which of you will narrate to us a hadith he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulation? Hudhayfah said: I will narrate to you as he said. He said: You are bold regarding it, so narrate. He said: The tribulation of a man regarding his family, his wealth, his child, and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, fasting, enjoining good, and forbidding evil. Umar said: I am not asking you about this; I am asking you about that which surges like the waves of the sea. He said: There is no harm for you in it, O Commander of the Faithful. Between you and it is a closed door. He said: Will it be opened or broken? He said: Rather it will be broken. He said: Then it will never be closed until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Isa except Ali ibn Abi Bakr."
"1778","1775 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Anas al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us from Qatadah and Humayd from Anas who said: People of Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Madinah unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to the milch camels of charity to drink from their milk. They drank until they recovered, then they killed the shepherd and drove off the camels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent in pursuit of them, they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ja'far except Salamah."
"1779","1776 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman from al-Sha'bi from Muhammad ibn Sayfi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the day of Ashura, so fast it, and whoever has eaten let him complete the rest of his day. And he sent to the villagers and those around Madinah of the Ansar, ordering them to fast the rest of their day."
"1780","1777 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Anas al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Sulayman ibn Buraydah from his father who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the times of prayer? He said: Pray with us these two days. He ordered Bilal when dawn broke and he called the adhan, then ordered him and he established (iqamah) and prayed. Then he ordered him and he called the adhan when the sun declined, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him and he called the adhan for Asr while the sun was high, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him and he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him when the twilight disappeared and he called the adhan for Isha', then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him the next day and he called the adhan for Fajr when dawn broke, then ordered him when it became bright and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him and he called the adhan for Zuhr when the shadow of everything became equal to it, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him when the shadow of everything became twice it and he called the adhan for Asr, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he ordered him and he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set, then ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he delayed Isha' until near a third of the night, then said: What is between these two is the time. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jarrah except Ali; Nuh alone narrated it."
"1781","1778 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nuh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us - (ha) - and he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak al-Kindi from Mahdi from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Illiyyun, one of them looks down upon Paradise, and his face shines for them as the moon shines for the people of this world on the night of the full moon, and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them and blessed. No one narrated this hadith from Mahdi except al-Jarrah; Ali ibn Abi Bakr alone narrated it."
"1782","1779 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Nuh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak from Abu Ishaq from Muslim ibn Nudhayr from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the muscle of my lower leg beneath it and said: This is the place of the lower garment; if you refuse, then lower than that; if you refuse, then the lower garment has no right in the ankles. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jarrah except Ali."
"1783","1780 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"1784","1781 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Umar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from al-Jarrah from al-A'mash from Umarah ibn Umayr, he said: Abu Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: I entered upon A'ishah, I and Masruq, and we said: Two men from the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them hastens the prayer and the breaking of the fast, and the other delays. She said: Which of them is the one who hastens the prayer and the breaking of the fast? We said: Ibn Mas'ud. She said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do."
"1785","1782 - And with the same chain: from al-A'mash from Muslim al-Batin from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother imposed upon herself the fast of a month, and she died without fulfilling it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If she had a debt, would you fulfill it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving of being fulfilled."
"1786","1783 - And with the same chain: from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously. He said: You are not like me; my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"1787","1784 - And with the same chain: from al-A'mash from Umarah ibn Umayr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Marry, O company of youths, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private parts, and whoever cannot, then fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"1788","1785 - And with the same chain: from al-Jarrah from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from A'ishah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"1789","1786 - And with the same chain: from al-Jarrah from Ibn Abi Layla from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting, between Makkah and Madinah."
"1790","1787 - And with the same chain: from al-Jarrah from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Ata' and Mujahid from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I broke my fast one day of Ramadan deliberately, and I had intercourse with my wife in it. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Offer a sacrificial camel. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Give charity of twenty sa' of dates, or nineteen, or twenty-one. He said: I cannot find. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing twenty sa' of dates, and he said: Give charity with this. He said: There is no household in Madinah more in need of it than us. He said: Then feed it to your family."
"1791","1788 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Qattan al-Baghdadi Abu Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi' al-Makki narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim al-Ahwal from Tawus from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two saffron-dyed garments on me and said: Did your mother command you with this? I said: Yes. He said: Then wash them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Umar."
"1792","1789 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Durays al-Faydi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Musa al-Madani narrated to us from Maslamah from Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Madani who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts three days of a sacred month: Thursday, Friday, and Saturday, there will be recorded for him the worship of two years. No one narrated this hadith from Maslamah except Ya'qub; Muhammad ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"1793","1790 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim from Sa'id except Isa."
"1794","1791 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muti' al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Salim from Ammar al-Hadrami from Zadham that Ali narrated a hadith, and a man belied him, so Ali said: I will supplicate against you if I spoke falsely. He said: Supplicate. So he supplicated against him, and he did not move until his sight was gone. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il except Hushaym."
"1795","1792 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril taught me upon one letter, and I kept asking him for more and he gave me more, until it ended at seven letters. Ibn Shihab said: The seven letters are only the matter when it is one, not differing in lawful or unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from the nephew of al-Zuhri except al-Darawardi."
"1796","1793 - Ahmad ibn Ali Abu al-Abbas al-Barbahari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz from Abdullah ibn Malik Ibn Buhaynah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Asr one day, and he stood in the two rak'ahs, then did not sit until he completed his prayer, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting."
"1797","1794 - And with the same chain: from al-Zuhri from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Zuhri except Ayyub."
"1798","1795 - And with the same chain: from Ayyub ibn Musa from Makhul from Irak ibn Malik from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no charity upon horses and slaves. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ibrahim and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"1799","1796 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the People of the Book was: (O People of the Book, come to a word equitable between us and you) to the end of the verse. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Shaybah."
"1800","1797 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died in my house, on my day, between my chest and my thigh, and (Allah) combined his saliva and my saliva. She said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr entered with a siwak in his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it, and I thought he would like to use it, so I took it, softened it, then handed it to him, and he brushed with it; I never saw a mouth better than it. Then he wanted to hand it to me, but his hand could not rise. When I saw that, I took it from him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibrahim."
